c3-f264-5a1d-a1ac-342ddb0d677e" :step/content 17592186247171 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147473 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a3269c43-47df-5acc-97bf-5a6fd7c5c99e" "question-4d03e717-deaf-523f-a995-dad5a2ef0024"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147198 :question/worked-solution "The number of infected files, $y(t),$ grows exponentially with a growth factor of $4.$\n\nLet's write down what we know:\n\n- $a = 10$ is the initial number of infected files\n\n- $b = 4$ is the growth factor (the number of infected files quadruples)\n\n- $t=$ the time (in hours)\n\nThe formula for exponential growth (in terms of a growth factor $b$) is\n\n$$\ny = ab^t.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct expression for $y(t)$ is\n\n$$\ny(t)= 10 \\cdot 4^{t}.\n$$\n\nTo find the number of files infected after $6$ hours, we  substitute $t=6$ into the above:\n\n$$\ny(6) = 10 \\cdot 4^{6} = 40\\,960\n$$\n\nTherefore, the computer will have $40\\,960$ infected files after $6$ hours." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147474 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a1c43e4b-f0c3-5827-a9fe-03d9f0ad0749" "question-3ef74434-74b6-5bd1-8d2d-3a97591fb1bc"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147199 :question/problem "In the week of opening, the grocery store sold $20$ kilograms of apples. After that, the weekly sales increased by $25 \\%$ every week. \n\nFind a function that models the total weight of apples sold in week $t$ after opening, and use this function to find the total amount of apples sold in the $4$th week." :question/worked-solution "The number of kilograms of apples sold $y(t)$ grows exponentially with a growth rate of $25 \\%.$\n\nLet's write down what we know:\n\n- $a = 20$ is the total weight of the apples (in kilograms) sold initially\n\n- $r = 0.25$ is the growth rate ($25 \\%$ expressed as a decimal)\n\n- $t=$ the time (in weeks) after opening\n\nThe formula for exponential growth (in terms of a growth rate $r$) is\n\n$$\ny = a(1+r)^t.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct expression for $y(t)$ is\n\n$$\ny   = 20 \\cdot (1 + 0.25)^{t}.\n$$\n\nSimplifying the above, we get\n\n$$\ny(t) = 20 \\cdot (1.25)^{t}.\n$$\n\nTo find the total weight of apples sold in week $4,$ we evaluate the above for $t=4\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\ny(4) = 20 \\cdot (1.25)^{4} \\approx 49\n$$\n\nTherefore, approximately $49$ kilograms of apples were sold in week $4.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147475 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0f781a71-78ec-54be-875d-95c07fb380d7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147215 :question/worked-solution "The number of listeners $L(t)$ grows exponentially with a growth rate of $190\\%.$\n\nLet's write down what we know:\n\n- $a = 80$ is the total number of listeners initially\n\n- $r = 1.9$ is the growth rate ($190\\%$ expressed as a decimal)\n\n- $t=$ the time (in weeks) after release\n\nThe formula for exponential growth is\n\n$$\nL = a(1+r)^t.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct expression for $L(t)$ is\n\n$$\nL = 80 \\cdot (1 + 1.9)^{t}.\n$$\n\nSimplifying the above, we get\n\n$$\nL(t) = 80 \\cdot (2.9)^{t}.\n$$\n\nTo find the total number of listeners after $2$ weeks, we evaluate the above for $t=2{:}$\n\n$$\nL(2) = 80 \\cdot (2.9)^{2} \\approx 673\n$$\n\nTherefore, the estimated number of listeners after $2$ weeks is $673.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-a3269c43-47df-5acc-97bf-5a6fd7c5c99e" :question/id #uuid "a3269c43-47df-5acc-97bf-5a6fd7c5c99e" :question/math-academy-id "q-103103" :question/problem "The number of bacteria $y(t)$ in a culture after $t$ hours is given by the following formula:\n\n$$\ny=\\text{___}\\cdot {5}^{t}\n$$\n\nIf the culture started with $7$ bacteria and this number increases fivefold every hour, then what is the missing value in the expression for $y?$" :question/worked-solution "The number of bacteria $y(t)$ grows exponentially with a growth factor of $5.$\n\nThe formula for exponential growth (in terms of the growth factor $b$) is\n\n$$\ny=a{b}^{t}.\n$$\n\nWe have:\n\n- $a=7$ is the initial number of bacteria.\n\n- $b=5$ is the growth factor (the number of bacteria increases fivefold every hour).\n\n- $t=$ the time, in hours.\n\nTherefore, the correct expression for $y$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =7\\cdot {5}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $7.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-044468b2-bf94-5551-bde4-fd78c33e877e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-044468b2-bf94-5551-bde4-fd78c33e877e" :answer-field/id #uuid "044468b2-bf94-5551-bde4-fd78c33e877e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e86c0f47-a4fd-56e0-8db9-ac7aded15688" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3eb4232f-556f-57a2-888b-432f46d7fa8b" "answer-e43f28f8-6ab9-5593-9ae7-16d8b9e7316a" "answer-e86c0f47-a4fd-56e0-8db9-ac7aded15688" "answer-c0d139d1-e0ec-52c5-9377-3fdeed0d175c" "answer-bc41e08e-82a6-5684-be54-6391754b72d2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3eb4232f-556f-57a2-888b-432f46d7fa8b" :answer/id #uuid "3eb4232f-556f-57a2-888b-432f46d7fa8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "35" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e43f28f8-6ab9-5593-9ae7-16d8b9e7316a" :answer/id #uuid "e43f28f8-6ab9-5593-9ae7-16d8b9e7316a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e86c0f47-a4fd-56e0-8db9-ac7aded15688" :answer/id #uuid "e86c0f47-a4fd-56e0-8db9-ac7aded15688" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c0d139d1-e0ec-52c5-9377-3fdeed0d175c" :answer/id #uuid "c0d139d1-e0ec-52c5-9377-3fdeed0d175c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bc41e08e-82a6-5684-be54-6391754b72d2" :answer/id #uuid "bc41e08e-82a6-5684-be54-6391754b72d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4d03e717-deaf-523f-a995-dad5a2ef0024" :question/id #uuid "4d03e717-deaf-523f-a995-dad5a2ef0024" :question/math-academy-id "q-63824" :question/problem "At the beginning of a study, there were $2\\,000$ ants in an anthill. The study shows that the number of ants doubles every month. What function represents the number of ants $y(t)$ after $t$ months?" :question/worked-solution "The number of ants $y(t)$ grows exponentially with a growth factor of $2.$\n\nThe formula for exponential growth (in terms of a growth factor $b$) is\n\n$$\ny=a{b}^{t}.\n$$\n\nWe have:\n\n- $a=2\\,000$ is the initial number of ants.\n\n- $b=2$ is the growth factor (the number of ants doubles every month).\n\n- $t=$ the time, in months.\n\nTherefore, the correct expression for $y(t)$ is\n\n$$\ny(t)=2\\,000\\cdot {2}^{t}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bed8a07f-b1e3-5291-93c3-eed235b080d0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bed8a07f-b1e3-5291-93c3-eed235b080d0" :answer-field/id #uuid "bed8a07f-b1e3-5291-93c3-eed235b080d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-dce4d0f7-0a32-5960-a13f-40ad332e5baf" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a1e651cf-8673-5d70-a5e0-df15771d9aef" "answer-0c42295e-f712-5a56-90ec-b9b3ab0ee9c9" "answer-dce4d0f7-0a32-5960-a13f-40ad332e5baf" "answer-14269be5-6f1d-50ca-9b8b-1b0e3e6814fc" "answer-8654440e-5fa6-5947-bc7d-7eab8ff3173b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a1e651cf-8673-5d70-a5e0-df15771d9aef" :answer/id #uuid "a1e651cf-8673-5d70-a5e0-df15771d9aef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)=(2\\,000\\cdot 2)^{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0c42295e-f712-5a56-90ec-b9b3ab0ee9c9" :answer/id #uuid "0c42295e-f712-5a56-90ec-b9b3ab0ee9c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)=2\\,000+{2}^{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dce4d0f7-0a32-5960-a13f-40ad332e5baf" :answer/id #uuid "dce4d0f7-0a32-5960-a13f-40ad332e5baf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)=2\\,000\\cdot {2}^{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-14269be5-6f1d-50ca-9b8b-1b0e3e6814fc" :answer/id #uuid "14269be5-6f1d-50ca-9b8b-1b0e3e6814fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)=2\\,{000}^{t}+{2}^{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8654440e-5fa6-5947-bc7d-7eab8ff3173b" :answer/id #uuid "8654440e-5fa6-5947-bc7d-7eab8ff3173b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)=2\\cdot (2\\,000)^{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a1c43e4b-f0c3-5827-a9fe-03d9f0ad0749" :question/id #uuid "a1c43e4b-f0c3-5827-a9fe-03d9f0ad0749" :question/math-academy-id "q-61866" :question/problem "There are $14$ bacteria in a culture. Every minute, the number of bacteria increases by $15%.$ What function represents the number of bacteria $y(t)$ after $t$ minutes?" :question/worked-solution "The number of bacteria $y(t)$ grows exponentially with a growth rate of $15%.$\n\nThe formula for exponential growth (in terms of a growth rate $r$) is\n\n$$\ny=a(1+r)^{t}.\n$$\n\nWe have:\n\n- $a=14$ is the initial number of bacteria.\n\n- $r=0.15$ is the growth rate ($15%$ expressed as a percent).\n\n- $t=$ the time, in minutes.\n\nTherefore, the correct expression for $y(t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =14\\cdot (1+0.15)^{t} \\\\  & =14\\cdot {1.15}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-09241892-4d92-5242-9af7-710ba5f70453"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-09241892-4d92-5242-9af7-710ba5f70453" :answer-field/id #uuid "09241892-4d92-5242-9af7-710ba5f70453" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-58af08ce-57e1-55c2-8835-a1c47b3d45c2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6a39807f-e0b0-55ac-8c7b-183b06419467" "answer-eaa68ffa-c31a-55a5-8217-a253d0cfd3ed" "answer-5f44ed35-a73d-59f9-a388-f6e2b4eae254" "answer-58af08ce-57e1-55c2-8835-a1c47b3d45c2" "answer-62742e47-d5f9-5a77-94a3-f21b87271f82"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6a39807f-e0b0-55ac-8c7b-183b06419467" :answer/id #uuid "6a39807f-e0b0-55ac-8c7b-183b06419467" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)=(14\\cdot 0.15)^{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eaa68ffa-c31a-55a5-8217-a253d0cfd3ed" :answer/id #uuid "eaa68ffa-c31a-55a5-8217-a253d0cfd3ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)=(14\\cdot 1.15)^{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5f44ed35-a73d-59f9-a388-f6e2b4eae254" :answer/id #uuid "5f44ed35-a73d-59f9-a388-f6e2b4eae254" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)=14\\cdot {0.15}^{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-58af08ce-57e1-55c2-8835-a1c47b3d45c2" :answer/id #uuid "58af08ce-57e1-55c2-8835-a1c47b3d45c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)=14\\cdot {1.15}^{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-62742e47-d5f9-5a77-94a3-f21b87271f82" :answer/id #uuid "62742e47-d5f9-5a77-94a3-f21b87271f82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)=14\\cdot {15}^{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3ef74434-74b6-5bd1-8d2d-3a97591fb1bc" :question/id #uuid "3ef74434-74b6-5bd1-8d2d-3a97591fb1bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-61657" :question/problem "A computer has $20$ files infected with a computer virus. The number of infected files $y(t)$ after $t$ days is given by the formula:\n\n$$\ny(t)=20\\cdot (\\text{___})^{t}\n$$\n\nIf the number of infected files increases $5%$ each day, then what is the missing value in the expression for $y?$" :question/worked-solution "The number of infected files $y(t)$ grows exponentially with a growth rate of $5%.$\n\nThe formula for exponential growth (in terms of a growth rate $r$) is\n\n$$\ny=a(1+r)^{t}.\n$$\n\nWe have:\n\n- $a=20$ is the initial number of infected files.\n\n- $r=0.05$ is the growth rate ($5%$ expressed as a decimal).\n\n- $t=$ the time, in days.\n\nTherefore, the correct expression for $y$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =20\\cdot (1+0.05)^{t} \\\\  & =20\\cdot (1.05)^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $1.05.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f5d48576-5f2c-576e-8f97-f11d75b1ee78"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f5d48576-5f2c-576e-8f97-f11d75b1ee78" :answer-field/id #uuid "f5d48576-5f2c-576e-8f97-f11d75b1ee78" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4d146dc1-99e1-5705-9fb0-9267e886095e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-56e051a7-8f0b-5466-b6d8-f334c4a74b11" "answer-247e479c-9bbc-5bbe-a0e3-0aae8ea1b13a" "answer-fd891c3d-5a7a-5876-86e9-682f7695882e" "answer-4d146dc1-99e1-5705-9fb0-9267e886095e" "answer-fb429f52-dc4a-587c-9a61-ace3e5f5c296"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-56e051a7-8f0b-5466-b6d8-f334c4a74b11" :answer/id #uuid "56e051a7-8f0b-5466-b6d8-f334c4a74b11" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.05" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-247e479c-9bbc-5bbe-a0e3-0aae8ea1b13a" :answer/id #uuid "247e479c-9bbc-5bbe-a0e3-0aae8ea1b13a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fd891c3d-5a7a-5876-86e9-682f7695882e" :answer/id #uuid "fd891c3d-5a7a-5876-86e9-682f7695882e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.95" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d146dc1-99e1-5705-9fb0-9267e886095e" :answer/id #uuid "4d146dc1-99e1-5705-9fb0-9267e886095e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.05" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb429f52-dc4a-587c-9a61-ace3e5f5c296" :answer/id #uuid "fb429f52-dc4a-587c-9a61-ace3e5f5c296" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-0f781a71-78ec-54be-875d-95c07fb380d7" :question/id #uuid "0f781a71-78ec-54be-875d-95c07fb380d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-318214" :question/problem "An online course launched with $100$ initial students. An exponential model estimates that at the end of each week after launch, the number of students increased by $160%$ of the number of students at the end of the previous week.\n\nAccording to this model, how many students are there estimated to be after $3$ weeks?" :question/worked-solution "The number of students $S(t)$ grows exponentially with a growth rate of $160%.$\n\nLet's write down what we know:\n\n- $a=100$ is the total number of students initially\n\n- $r=1.6$ is the growth rate ($160%$ expressed as a decimal)\n\n- $t=$ the time (in weeks) after the launch\n\nThe formula for exponential growth is\n\n$$\nS=a(1+r)^{t}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct expression for $S(t)$ is\n\n$$\nS=100\\cdot (1+1.6)^{t}.\n$$\n\nSimplifying the above, we get\n\n$$\nS(t)=100\\cdot (2.6)^{t}.\n$$\n\nTo find the total number of students after $3$ weeks, we evaluate the above for $t=3:$\n\n$$\nS(3)=100\\cdot (2.6)^{3}≈1758\n$$\n\nTherefore, the estimated number of students after $3$ weeks is $1758.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9b4c7c93-453d-5bac-b606-f82c34cb377d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9b4c7c93-453d-5bac-b606-f82c34cb377d" :answer-field/id #uuid "9b4c7c93-453d-5bac-b606-f82c34cb377d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3ca45b50-aa83-548f-8093-7884f91372f8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-360767c6-d66d-5903-9180-b0da4415a5dc" "answer-bc6abb1b-3487-54e7-bdd5-09377dd6493c" "answer-3ca45b50-aa83-548f-8093-7884f91372f8" "answer-ad1a9c65-fa8c-5d77-8312-c62177840ed0" "answer-6d3bbde6-9914-5283-a9d6-322d06b9ef0b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-360767c6-d66d-5903-9180-b0da4415a5dc" :answer/id #uuid "360767c6-d66d-5903-9180-b0da4415a5dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1506" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bc6abb1b-3487-54e7-bdd5-09377dd6493c" :answer/id #uuid "bc6abb1b-3487-54e7-bdd5-09377dd6493c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "160" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3ca45b50-aa83-548f-8093-7884f91372f8" :answer/id #uuid "3ca45b50-aa83-548f-8093-7884f91372f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1758" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ad1a9c65-fa8c-5d77-8312-c62177840ed0" :answer/id #uuid "ad1a9c65-fa8c-5d77-8312-c62177840ed0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1962" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6d3bbde6-9914-5283-a9d6-322d06b9ef0b" :answer/id #uuid "6d3bbde6-9914-5283-a9d6-322d06b9ef0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "410" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147767 :question/worked-solution "The number of views $V(t)$ grows exponentially with a growth rate of $250%.$\n\nLet's write down what we know:\n\n- $a=90$ is the total number of views initially\n\n- $r=2.5$ is the growth rate ($250%$ expressed as a decimal)\n\n- $t=$ the time (in hours) after upload\n\nThe formula for exponential growth is\n\n$$\nV=a(1+r)^{t}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct expression for $V(t)$ is\n\n$$\nV=90\\cdot (1+2.5)^{t}.\n$$\n\nSimplifying the above, we get\n\n$$\nV(t)=90\\cdot (3.5)^{t}.\n$$\n\nTo find the total number of views after $3$ hours, we evaluate the above for $t=3:$\n\n$$\nV(3)=90\\cdot (3.5)^{3}≈3859\n$$\n\nTherefore, the estimated number of views after $3$ hours is $3859.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186144303 :answer-field/correct 17592186144304 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186148684 :tutorial/content "Suppose that there are $120$ deer in a wildlife reserve. If the deer population doubles every year, can we find a function that gives the number of deer after $t$ years? \n\nFirst, let's write down what we know:\n\n- $a = 120$ is the **initial number** of deer\n\n- $b =2$ is the **growth factor** (equal to $2$ because the number of deer doubles every year)\n\n- $t=$ the time (in years)\n\nWe let $y(t)$ be the number of deer in the reserve after $t$ years.  The formula for $y(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\ny(t) = ab^t.\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values for $a$ and $b,$ we get\n\n$$\ny(t) = 120\\cdot 2^t.\n$$\n\nWe can use this formula to find the number of deer in the reserve for any value of $t \\geq 0.$ For example, to find the number of deer after $3$ years, we substitute $t=3$ into the function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(3) & =120\\cdot {2}^{3} \\\\  & =120\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =960\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo there will be $960$ deer after $3$ years.\n\nFinally, notice that substituting $t=0$ into the formula gives the initial number of deer:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =120\\cdot {2}^{0} \\\\  & =120\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =120\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186148683 :tutorial/content "When dealing with exponential growth, it's more common to be given a **growth rate** instead of a growth factor. A growth rate is usually expressed as a percent.\n\nFor example, suppose that an investor invests $\\[math]500$ dollars in the shares of some high-growth companies. It's expected that the investment will grow by $35\\%$ each year. Can we write a function that describes the value of the investment after $t$ years? \n\nLet's write down what we know:\n\n- $a=\\[/math]500$ is the **initial value** of the investment\n\n- $r = 0.35$ is the **growth rate** (this is simply $35\\%$ expressed as a decimal)\n\n- $t$ is the time (in years)\n\nLet $y(t)$ be the value of the investment after $t$ years. The formula for $y(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\ny = a(1+r)^t.\n$$\n\nSubstituting in our values for $a$ and $r,$ we get\n\n$$\ny(t) = 500(1+0.35)^t.\n$$\n\nSimplifying the above, we arrive at\n\n$$\ny(t) = 500(1.35)^t.\n$$\n\nWhen creating exponential growth functions, the key takeaway is this:\n\n- If you're given a **growth rate** $r$ (usually expressed as a percent), then use the formula $y = a(1+r)^t.$\n\n- If you're given a **growth factor** $b,$ then use the formula $y = ab^t.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147671 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064305 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-180b64b1-b15e-57ee-9a92-ff79a509bb19" "question-f02573a0-2790-58d2-b6cc-7bac38c415b0" "question-7c4e2820-92a5-519d-9225-25cc4948f0c9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-180b64b1-b15e-57ee-9a92-ff79a509bb19" :question/id #uuid "180b64b1-b15e-57ee-9a92-ff79a509bb19" :question/math-academy-id "q-129431" :question/problem "$\\sqrt{{a}^{2}{b}^{2}}=$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the square root of a perfect square can be simplified using absolute value.\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{{x}^{2}}=|x|\n$$\n\nAlso, we notice that ${a}^{2}$ and ${b}^{2}$ are perfect squares.\n\nFirst, we write the expression under the square root as a perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{a}^{2}{b}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{a\\cdot a\\cdot b\\cdot b} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{a\\cdot b\\cdot a\\cdot b} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(ab)\\cdot (ab)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(ab)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the absolute value of the squared quantity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{(ab)^{2}} & =|ab|\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e9a1e499-9cd1-5d15-a079-6c7d6a1a34e4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e9a1e499-9cd1-5d15-a079-6c7d6a1a34e4" :answer-field/id #uuid "e9a1e499-9cd1-5d15-a079-6c7d6a1a34e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a8914752-237a-5f09-b64c-97f60b10586b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1aec2d0b-0038-5b9d-8e4f-821e3fd956b9" "answer-677e43b4-9e76-52a3-a1bb-1004c237476a" "answer-99522d80-934c-58f8-8645-3e3d69f47b0b" "answer-a8914752-237a-5f09-b64c-97f60b10586b" "answer-9f014637-b6bb-5d87-a79d-711ebb7c4222"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1aec2d0b-0038-5b9d-8e4f-821e3fd956b9" :answer/id #uuid "1aec2d0b-0038-5b9d-8e4f-821e3fd956b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm ab" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-677e43b4-9e76-52a3-a1bb-1004c237476a" :answer/id #uuid "677e43b4-9e76-52a3-a1bb-1004c237476a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "ab" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-99522d80-934c-58f8-8645-3e3d69f47b0b" :answer/id #uuid "99522d80-934c-58f8-8645-3e3d69f47b0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a|b|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8914752-237a-5f09-b64c-97f60b10586b" :answer/id #uuid "a8914752-237a-5f09-b64c-97f60b10586b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|ab|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f014637-b6bb-5d87-a79d-711ebb7c4222" :answer/id #uuid "9f014637-b6bb-5d87-a79d-711ebb7c4222" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|a|b" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f02573a0-2790-58d2-b6cc-7bac38c415b0" :question/id #uuid "f02573a0-2790-58d2-b6cc-7bac38c415b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-129432" :question/problem "$\\sqrt{{y}^{2}{z}^{2}}=$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the square root of a perfect square can be simplified using absolute value.\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{{x}^{2}}=|x|\n$$\n\nAlso, we notice that ${y}^{2}$ and ${z}^{2}$ are perfect squares.\n\nFirst, we write the expression under the square root as a perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{y}^{2}{z}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{y\\cdot y\\cdot z\\cdot z} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{y\\cdot z\\cdot y\\cdot z} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(yz)\\cdot (yz)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(yz)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the absolute value of the squared quantity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{(yz)^{2}} & =|yz|\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c670e448-1e22-5196-8fb8-d4e5db38967e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c670e448-1e22-5196-8fb8-d4e5db38967e" :answer-field/id #uuid "c670e448-1e22-5196-8fb8-d4e5db38967e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-307e1365-05e4-5bc5-a68f-ed2c32a38c7b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-20c639d7-7a27-579c-9de2-bfc34b74a330" "answer-ef935ffb-6785-53bf-9c0d-9df9b9b9ef91" "answer-2c490ecf-5f63-5a62-a464-1073d7062fec" "answer-484f6643-41cd-55bf-ae3f-2f1cfc9ad32a" "answer-307e1365-05e4-5bc5-a68f-ed2c32a38c7b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-20c639d7-7a27-579c-9de2-bfc34b74a330" :answer/id #uuid "20c639d7-7a27-579c-9de2-bfc34b74a330" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-yz" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ef935ffb-6785-53bf-9c0d-9df9b9b9ef91" :answer/id #uuid "ef935ffb-6785-53bf-9c0d-9df9b9b9ef91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm yz" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2c490ecf-5f63-5a62-a464-1073d7062fec" :answer/id #uuid "2c490ecf-5f63-5a62-a464-1073d7062fec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "yz" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-484f6643-41cd-55bf-ae3f-2f1cfc9ad32a" :answer/id #uuid "484f6643-41cd-55bf-ae3f-2f1cfc9ad32a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y|z|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-307e1365-05e4-5bc5-a68f-ed2c32a38c7b" :answer/id #uuid "307e1365-05e4-5bc5-a68f-ed2c32a38c7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|yz|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7c4e2820-92a5-519d-9225-25cc4948f0c9" :question/id #uuid "7c4e2820-92a5-519d-9225-25cc4948f0c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-129436" :question/problem "$\\sqrt{121{c}^{2}{d}^{2}}=$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the square root of a perfect square can be simplified using absolute value.\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{{x}^{2}}=|x|\n$$\n\nAlso, we notice that $121,{c}^{2},$ and ${d}^{2}$ are perfect squares.\n\nFirst, we write the expression under the square root as a perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{121{c}^{2}{d}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{{11}^{2}\\cdot {c}^{2}\\cdot {d}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{11\\cdot 11\\cdot c\\cdot c\\cdot d\\cdot d} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{11\\cdot c\\cdot d\\cdot 11\\cdot c\\cdot d} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(11cd)\\cdot (11cd)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(11cd)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the absolute value of the squared quantity and simplify using the rules of absolute value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{(11cd)^{2}} & =|11cd| \\\\  & =|11|\\cdot |cd| \\\\  & =11|cd|\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f8e5500d-4d6c-5ee8-8d88-044948dcf393"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f8e5500d-4d6c-5ee8-8d88-044948dcf393" :answer-field/id #uuid "f8e5500d-4d6c-5ee8-8d88-044948dcf393" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6fb06393-6aac-50f5-a04b-9283e7529b0f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f133a350-9010-5f13-9ae6-3042c70926c3" "answer-efc7ea96-0e54-53a9-8e3a-8267aca4bace" "answer-6fb06393-6aac-50f5-a04b-9283e7529b0f" "answer-d516194b-16c2-53ca-ab0c-da1f099bf768" "answer-da17cde0-38b7-57ed-9d96-55cb435c49c5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f133a350-9010-5f13-9ae6-3042c70926c3" :answer/id #uuid "f133a350-9010-5f13-9ae6-3042c70926c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11cd" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-efc7ea96-0e54-53a9-8e3a-8267aca4bace" :answer/id #uuid "efc7ea96-0e54-53a9-8e3a-8267aca4bace" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11c|d|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6fb06393-6aac-50f5-a04b-9283e7529b0f" :answer/id #uuid "6fb06393-6aac-50f5-a04b-9283e7529b0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11|cd|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d516194b-16c2-53ca-ab0c-da1f099bf768" :answer/id #uuid "d516194b-16c2-53ca-ab0c-da1f099bf768" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11|c|d" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-da17cde0-38b7-57ed-9d96-55cb435c49c5" :answer/id #uuid "da17cde0-38b7-57ed-9d96-55cb435c49c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm 11cd" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-a131be7b-68d2-57db-b50e-5c3bbbbafaae" :activity/id #uuid "a131be7b-68d2-57db-b50e-5c3bbbbafaae" :activity/title "The Square Root of a Perfect Square With Algebraic Expressions" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049843 :activity/course 17592186046648 :activity/steps ["step-830fe1f9-792b-5b8c-98b4-ab430e7693d7" "step-580c91a1-4c77-59fd-b9e9-6a409f2c4647" "step-71d5e5ee-5255-55c6-92c2-3b6a9653dcc6"] :activity/first-step "step-830fe1f9-792b-5b8c-98b4-ab430e7693d7" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-830fe1f9-792b-5b8c-98b4-ab430e7693d7" :step/id #uuid "830fe1f9-792b-5b8c-98b4-ab430e7693d7" :step/content "question-180b64b1-b15e-57ee-9a92-ff79a509bb19" :step/next "step-580c91a1-4c77-59fd-b9e9-6a409f2c4647" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-580c91a1-4c77-59fd-b9e9-6a409f2c4647" :step/id #uuid "580c91a1-4c77-59fd-b9e9-6a409f2c4647" :step/content "question-f02573a0-2790-58d2-b6cc-7bac38c415b0" :step/next "step-71d5e5ee-5255-55c6-92c2-3b6a9653dcc6" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-71d5e5ee-5255-55c6-92c2-3b6a9653dcc6" :step/id #uuid "71d5e5ee-5255-55c6-92c2-3b6a9653dcc6" :step/content "question-7c4e2820-92a5-519d-9225-25cc4948f0c9" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147563 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-38bb781d-e24d-5ca2-821e-7901089bd6a3" "question-978bca7b-e158-5bd2-ae01-fa65d0556739"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-38bb781d-e24d-5ca2-821e-7901089bd6a3" :question/id #uuid "38bb781d-e24d-5ca2-821e-7901089bd6a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-45601" :question/problem "The area of an oil patch, measured in square kilometers, is given by the function $A(t)=10\\cdot (1.1)^{t}$, where $t$ is the time in days since the pollution occurred. How many square kilometers does the area increase by between day $1$ and day $2?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the growth of the patch between day $1$ and day $2$, we need to subtract the area after day $1$ from the area after day $2.$ So we need to calculate\n\n$$\nA(2)-A(1).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the area after the first day, $A(1)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A(1) & =10\\cdot (1.1)^{1} \\\\  & =10\\cdot 1.1 \\\\  & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find $A(2),$ the area after the second day:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A(2) & =10\\cdot (1.1)^{2} \\\\  & =10\\cdot 1.21 \\\\  & =12.1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the growth of the patch between day $1$ and day $2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A(2)-A(1) & =12.1-11=1.1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the area increased by $1.1$ square kilometer between day $1$ and day $2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1bf52d0f-f83a-5aa3-b11c-feea28b4ef8a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1bf52d0f-f83a-5aa3-b11c-feea28b4ef8a" :answer-field/id #uuid "1bf52d0f-f83a-5aa3-b11c-feea28b4ef8a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7ca68bbc-a218-5b0c-a014-725824cd865d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7ca68bbc-a218-5b0c-a014-725824cd865d" "answer-bc8370e9-2478-56a9-9b58-f413970d8e02" "answer-01c8a340-3d84-5653-a1c7-a6b291ebaf8b" "answer-2888b44b-0869-5796-ade9-2cdfc7016b90" "answer-782c49fd-1ec9-542f-9446-c12766d3d684"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7ca68bbc-a218-5b0c-a014-725824cd865d" :answer/id #uuid "7ca68bbc-a218-5b0c-a014-725824cd865d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.1\\,{\\text{km}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bc8370e9-2478-56a9-9b58-f413970d8e02" :answer/id #uuid "bc8370e9-2478-56a9-9b58-f413970d8e02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10\\,{\\text{km}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-01c8a340-3d84-5653-a1c7-a6b291ebaf8b" :answer/id #uuid "01c8a340-3d84-5653-a1c7-a6b291ebaf8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11\\,{\\text{km}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2888b44b-0869-5796-ade9-2cdfc7016b90" :answer/id #uuid "2888b44b-0869-5796-ade9-2cdfc7016b90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12.1\\,{\\text{km}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-782c49fd-1ec9-542f-9446-c12766d3d684" :answer/id #uuid "782c49fd-1ec9-542f-9446-c12766d3d684" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.1\\,{\\text{km}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-978bca7b-e158-5bd2-ae01-fa65d0556739" :question/id #uuid "978bca7b-e158-5bd2-ae01-fa65d0556739" :question/math-academy-id "q-45697" :question/problem "The population $M(t)$ of a colony of rodents is given by $M(t)=1\\,000\\cdot (1.6)^{t}$, where $t$ is the time in years since the beginning of the observations. How many additional rodents will be born in the colony between years $2$ and $3?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the growth in the population of rodents between year $2$ and year $3$, we need to subtract the population after year $2$ from the population after year $3.$ So we need to calculate\n\n$$\nM(3)-M(2).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the population after the second year, $M(2)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M(2) & =1\\,000\\cdot (1.6)^{(2)} \\\\  & =1\\,000\\cdot 2.56 \\\\  & =2\\,560\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find $M(3),$ the population after the third year:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M(3) & =1\\,000\\cdot (1.6)^{(3)} \\\\  & =1\\,000\\cdot 4.096 \\\\  & =4\\,096\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the growth in the population between year $2$ and year $3$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M(3)-M(2) & =4\\,096-2\\,560=1\\,536.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the population of rodents increased by $1\\,536$ between years $2$ and $3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d469c932-3585-58b1-be22-0b73b73c3ef8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d469c932-3585-58b1-be22-0b73b73c3ef8" :answer-field/id #uuid "d469c932-3585-58b1-be22-0b73b73c3ef8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-292544c4-976c-5a08-ba6c-8e830e5ab925" :answer-field/choices ["answer-292544c4-976c-5a08-ba6c-8e830e5ab925" "answer-18adfc4b-40de-5736-b8ad-16bd94bf6b24" "answer-929acbf8-3e5b-5715-a98b-c7c7b5f2beba" "answer-036eafb8-c49d-58cf-aba0-dbb85b8a6d63" "answer-19915433-b6de-5ef5-93c0-b49e9f51d44a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-292544c4-976c-5a08-ba6c-8e830e5ab925" :answer/id #uuid "292544c4-976c-5a08-ba6c-8e830e5ab925" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,536" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-18adfc4b-40de-5736-b8ad-16bd94bf6b24" :answer/id #uuid "18adfc4b-40de-5736-b8ad-16bd94bf6b24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,653" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-929acbf8-3e5b-5715-a98b-c7c7b5f2beba" :answer/id #uuid "929acbf8-3e5b-5715-a98b-c7c7b5f2beba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,460" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-036eafb8-c49d-58cf-aba0-dbb85b8a6d63" :answer/id #uuid "036eafb8-c49d-58cf-aba0-dbb85b8a6d63" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,560" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-19915433-b6de-5ef5-93c0-b49e9f51d44a" :answer/id #uuid "19915433-b6de-5ef5-93c0-b49e9f51d44a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\,096" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147572 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-065bbf88-3b11-5079-b0c1-f463dc0506a1"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-065bbf88-3b11-5079-b0c1-f463dc0506a1" :question/id #uuid "065bbf88-3b11-5079-b0c1-f463dc0506a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-64102" :question/problem "The total area, in square meters,  covered by blueberry bushes in a forest can be modeled by the expression $800\\cdot (1.1)^{t},$ where $t$ is the number of years since the year $2015.$ What does the base of the exponential expression $(1.1)$ mean in this context?" :question/worked-solution "The answer choices require interpretation as a percent, and so we use the growth rate formula.\n\nThe given expression is an exponential growth expression of the form $y(t)=a\\cdot (1+r)^{t}$, where:\n\n- $a=800$ represents the initial area covered by the  blueberry bushes\n\n- $1+r=1.1,$ where $r$ is the growth rate\n\n- $t$ is the number of years since $2015$\n\nSolving for $r$:\n\n$$\n1+r=1.1\\,⟹\\,r=0.1\n$$\n\nNow, $0.1$ (expressed as a percent) is equal to $10%.$ Therefore, the area covered by the bushes grows at a rate of $10%$ per year." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-365bcff0-9da9-51b5-b700-1716404308aa"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-365bcff0-9da9-51b5-b700-1716404308aa" :answer-field/id #uuid "365bcff0-9da9-51b5-b700-1716404308aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-90b44fdb-a8cc-514c-95fd-f7202dd8720f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fdfb7f6b-b500-55a3-b9aa-cd8cc691d7b6" "answer-90b44fdb-a8cc-514c-95fd-f7202dd8720f" "answer-1e8344b2-9e67-5157-94a5-d4ffcc91bb42" "answer-bc4ad3b6-0cd3-5e75-bd2f-774f75c48689" "answer-b4c80e48-faec-5b72-aef4-f19de49c3f3f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fdfb7f6b-b500-55a3-b9aa-cd8cc691d7b6" :answer/id #uuid "fdfb7f6b-b500-55a3-b9aa-cd8cc691d7b6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The area covered by the bushes grows at a rate of $1.1%$ per year" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-90b44fdb-a8cc-514c-95fd-f7202dd8720f" :answer/id #uuid "90b44fdb-a8cc-514c-95fd-f7202dd8720f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The area covered by the bushes grows at a rate of $10%$ per year" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1e8344b2-9e67-5157-94a5-d4ffcc91bb42" :answer/id #uuid "1e8344b2-9e67-5157-94a5-d4ffcc91bb42" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The area covered by the bushes grows at a rate of $11%$ per year" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bc4ad3b6-0cd3-5e75-bd2f-774f75c48689" :answer/id #uuid "bc4ad3b6-0cd3-5e75-bd2f-774f75c48689" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The area covered by the bushes grows at a rate of $8%$ per year" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b4c80e48-faec-5b72-aef4-f19de49c3f3f" :answer/id #uuid "b4c80e48-faec-5b72-aef4-f19de49c3f3f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The area covered by the bushes increases by a factor of $1.1$ every $8$ years" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-e9225a93-dc03-57da-bec9-4f535a279d72" :activity/id #uuid "e9225a93-dc03-57da-bec9-4f535a279d72" :activity/title "Interpreting Exponential Growth" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048650 :activity/course 17592186046648 :activity/steps ["step-c81e5c67-ac42-5acf-b9ba-dd9c76587fb0" "step-92b6b921-bfab-5106-aebc-d9c7e4e38733" "step-b2e8828f-e8f0-5f6b-8f2a-4544652c7ffc"] :activity/first-step "step-c81e5c67-ac42-5acf-b9ba-dd9c76587fb0" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-c81e5c67-ac42-5acf-b9ba-dd9c76587fb0" :step/id #uuid "c81e5c67-ac42-5acf-b9ba-dd9c76587fb0" :step/content "question-38bb781d-e24d-5ca2-821e-7901089bd6a3" :step/next "step-92b6b921-bfab-5106-aebc-d9c7e4e38733" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-92b6b921-bfab-5106-aebc-d9c7e4e38733" :step/id #uuid "92b6b921-bfab-5106-aebc-d9c7e4e38733" :step/content "question-978bca7b-e158-5bd2-ae01-fa65d0556739" :step/next "step-b2e8828f-e8f0-5f6b-8f2a-4544652c7ffc" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-b2e8828f-e8f0-5f6b-8f2a-4544652c7ffc" :step/id #uuid "b2e8828f-e8f0-5f6b-8f2a-4544652c7ffc" :step/content "question-065bbf88-3b11-5079-b0c1-f463dc0506a1" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162157 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8283d19d-ef90-50f2-bc41-5e0573a21b42" "question-993667c9-c973-5dd1-b35f-eb1848f951dd"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162158 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-03070e45-f0e3-5991-b98c-709745709961" "question-c7f8c921-7225-588c-b9e8-a78affb7e519"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162159 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-fd9f0c45-62d6-5bab-b897-93c9f4793a8e" "question-42308119-ffcd-55c6-b052-68e017e7cc90"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162529 :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined as\n\n$$\nA=\\{\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}+1}:n\\in \\{1,2,3,4\\}\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the supremum of $A?$\n\n$sup(A)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The supremum of a set $A$ is the smallest upper bound of $A.$\n\nIf $A$ is a finite set, the supremum of $A$ equals its maximum. \n\nFirst, let's write down all the terms of our set by substituting $n=1,2,3,4$ into the expression for the elements of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(-1)^{1}}{(1)^{2}+1} & =-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{(-1)^{2}}{(2)^{2}+1} & =\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ \\frac{(-1)^{3}}{(3)^{2}+1} & =-\\frac{1}{10} \\\\ \\frac{(-1)^{4}}{(4)^{2}+1} & =\\frac{1}{17}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nA=\\{-\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\frac{1}{5},\\,-\\frac{1}{10},\\,\\frac{1}{17}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sup(A) & =max\\{-\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\frac{1}{5},\\,-\\frac{1}{10},\\,\\frac{1}{17}\\}=\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186160501 :answer-field/correct "answer-d8929061-a36b-574c-a4a0-2a9230b65f4c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d8929061-a36b-574c-a4a0-2a9230b65f4c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d8929061-a36b-574c-a4a0-2a9230b65f4c" :answer/id #uuid "d8929061-a36b-574c-a4a0-2a9230b65f4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162525 :question/problem "What is the infimum of the set $A=\\{0,\\,3,\\,6,\\,9\\}?$\n\n$inf(A)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The infimum of a set $A$ is the greatest lower bound of $A.$\n\nIf $A$ is a finite set, the infimum of $A$ equals its minimum. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}inf(A) & =min\\{0,\\,3,\\,6,\\,9\\}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186160485 :answer-field/correct "answer-b400c16c-d465-56c8-b68a-91d91b2bf06e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b400c16c-d465-56c8-b68a-91d91b2bf06e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b400c16c-d465-56c8-b68a-91d91b2bf06e" :answer/id #uuid "b400c16c-d465-56c8-b68a-91d91b2bf06e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8283d19d-ef90-50f2-bc41-5e0573a21b42" :question/id #uuid "8283d19d-ef90-50f2-bc41-5e0573a21b42" :question/math-academy-id "q-253512" :question/problem "Consider the set $A=(0,2).$ Complete the following reasoning to identify $sup(A).$\n\nThe supremum of a set $A$ is the {{field-1}} of $A.$\n\nThe set of upper bounds of $A$ is as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{x\\in R\\,:\\,x{{field-2}}{{field-3}}\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "The supremum of a set $A$ is the smallest upper bound of $A.$\n\nTo find the supremum of this set, we must find the set containing **all** upper bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of upper bounds) and take the minimum of this set.\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n- Any number in the set $x\\ge 2$ is greater than or equal to the elements of $A.$ Thus, the set $[2,\\infty )$ contains only upper bounds of $A.$\n\n- Any number in the set $x<2$ is **not** an upper bound of $A.$ In other words, we can always find an element of $A$ that is greater than $x$ for any $x<2.$\n\nTherefore, $[2,\\infty )$ is the set of upper bounds of $A,$ and\n\n$$\nsup(A)=min[2,\\infty )=2.\n$$\n\nNotice that $2\\notin A.$\n\nThe completed reasoning is given below.\n\nThe supremum of $A$ is the $\\text{smallest upper bound}$ of $A.$\n\nThe set of upper bounds of $A$ is as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{x\\in R\\,:\\,x\\ge 2\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $sup(A)=2\\notin A.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-735af475-5f6e-5f4d-94ac-fce00a40be32" "answer-field-97af60c6-81d5-5dcc-8fd8-64c597a89cac" "answer-field-cfc061c6-f499-57fc-948d-02e770903359" "answer-field-c36b9a2c-4e62-5b21-9012-7faf214bd6f7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-735af475-5f6e-5f4d-94ac-fce00a40be32" :answer-field/id #uuid "735af475-5f6e-5f4d-94ac-fce00a40be32" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-f409a862-986f-5f72-b38f-9785d600adce" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2ae27d87-d1eb-5508-9fca-440370a0760d" "answer-acc9f243-7017-5914-9e36-38110bd0f43d" "answer-fb1c810a-8c08-59ba-b916-0dd9d63ae793" "answer-f409a862-986f-5f72-b38f-9785d600adce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2ae27d87-d1eb-5508-9fca-440370a0760d" :answer/id #uuid "2ae27d87-d1eb-5508-9fca-440370a0760d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "greatest lower bound" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-acc9f243-7017-5914-9e36-38110bd0f43d" :answer/id #uuid "acc9f243-7017-5914-9e36-38110bd0f43d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "greatest upper bound" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb1c810a-8c08-59ba-b916-0dd9d63ae793" :answer/id #uuid "fb1c810a-8c08-59ba-b916-0dd9d63ae793" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "smallest lower bound" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f409a862-986f-5f72-b38f-9785d600adce" :answer/id #uuid "f409a862-986f-5f72-b38f-9785d600adce" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "smallest upper bound" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-97af60