:\\,x{{field-2}}{{field-3}}\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "The infimum of $A$ is the greatest lower bound of $A.$\n\nTo find the infimum of this set, we must find the set containing **all** lower bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of lower bounds) and take the maximum of this set.\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n- Any number in the set $x\\le -5$ is smaller than or equal to the elements of $A.$ Thus, the set $(-\\infty ,-5]$ contains only lower bounds of $A.$\n\n- Any number in the set $x>-5$ is **not** a lower bound of $A.$ In other words, we can always find an element of $A$ that is smaller than $x$ for any $x>-5.$\n\nTherefore, $(-\\infty ,-5]$ is the set of lower bounds of $A,$ and\n\n$$\ninf(A)=max(-\\infty ,-5]=-5.\n$$\n\nNotice that $-5\\notin A.$\n\nThe completed reasoning is given below.\n\nThe infimum of $A$ is the $\\text{greatest lower bound}$ of $A.$\n\nThe set of lower bounds of $A$ is as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{x\\in R\\,:\\,x\\le -5\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $inf(A)=-5\\notin A.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-efa87f6a-f0a6-55ea-84b0-cbaaaa5fa7b9" "answer-field-d6c45689-30e7-585c-ad39-8fbbfb0111be" "answer-field-e67fda2f-7168-5347-a8d3-f53e8a1874eb" "answer-field-1e6ccc5e-e2f1-5031-9908-8c3a1cc535d6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-efa87f6a-f0a6-55ea-84b0-cbaaaa5fa7b9" :answer-field/id #uuid "efa87f6a-f0a6-55ea-84b0-cbaaaa5fa7b9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-a21eac77-4a8d-5a1a-a8b3-704e5197e4df" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a21eac77-4a8d-5a1a-a8b3-704e5197e4df" "answer-225422b7-65e9-5615-8767-2543d225f63d" "answer-b2347c38-baed-5481-b764-dca5a77c4889" "answer-d62ffa3e-3570-5c8f-89e2-cacd170877a5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a21eac77-4a8d-5a1a-a8b3-704e5197e4df" :answer/id #uuid "a21eac77-4a8d-5a1a-a8b3-704e5197e4df" :answer/type :answer.type/text 