8a-5567-556e-812e-8c8f5c7c8f4e" :step/content "question-7a8715ea-a6b5-5612-a604-9c2ef5fe8cee" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179652 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-62541dad-de47-58c3-a80c-47be806ee721" "question-92babace-3fcf-5d4a-8789-c7e1f3a12026"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-62541dad-de47-58c3-a80c-47be806ee721" :question/id #uuid "62541dad-de47-58c3-a80c-47be806ee721" :question/math-academy-id "q-235959" :question/problem "![](images/2d/2d46569e841a4bd7cf6646788f7bb5aec88a2386f96b8614ffec3e9c055bc200.png)\n\nWhat is the range of the function $f(x),$ shown above?\n\n$\\,$  The range is $f(x)\\in $\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "We find the ranges of the individual pieces, and then calculate their union:\n\n- The range of the branch defined on $x\\in [-3,0)$ is $[0,2)$\n\n- The range of the branch defined on $x\\in [0,3]$ is $[-3,-1]$\n\nTherefore, the range of $f(x)$ is $[-3,-1]\\cup [0,2).$\n\n**Note:** From the graph, we see that the value $y=2$ is NOT a valid output of the function $y=f(x).$ Therefore, we use parentheses $(…)$ instead of brackets $[…]$ at this endpoint." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0475e577-c65b-5fdd-847b-25cee8140b7d" "answer-field-f9d5cf43-46d1-5177-8e2d-2002b8fcbaa2" "answer-field-c3a27fb8-358f-526c-99e2-e939fb691eef"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0475e577-c65b-5fdd-847b-25cee8140b7d" :answer-field/id #uuid "0475e577-c65b-5fdd-847b-25cee8140b7d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-090f6b0d-954f-59b1-8627-6b16913c1f7d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b22f6f36-3dde-51a4-a64b-073f992e2909" "answer-63672e31-cac6-5da3-a745-b0ce239264df" "answer-f9e00e11-d23c-50d4-bca3-793cebab7b6b" "answer-090f6b0d-954f-59b1-8627-6b16913c1f7d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b22f6f36-3dde-51a4-a64b-073f992e2909"