36 :question/problem "What is the range of the function $h$ defined by the following table?\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $-2$ | $3$ | $-4$ | $5$ | $-6$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $h(x)$ | $-7$ | $6$ | $-5$ | $4$ | $-3$ | $6$ | $-1$ | $0$ |" :question/worked-solution "The range of $h(x)$ consists of all the outputs that have a corresponding $x$-input.\n\nIn a table, the range consists of all numbers that feature in the row corresponding to $h(x).$\n\nTherefore, the range is the set $\\{-7,-5,-3,-1,0,4,6\\}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186082547 :answer-field/correct "answer-86108145-1c61-593e-9944-c48c2d3ee18a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-84cac5ce-e3e7-5c21-8c31-79b4eac65790" "answer-9e8e1400-45eb-5e9a-b750-f95f072133d5" "answer-e84fe7fd-6735-5887-8811-1577bf7dc94a" "answer-86108145-1c61-593e-9944-c48c2d3ee18a" "answer-f0a977cc-2b1a-5047-8a3c-d6058da4b075"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84cac5ce-e3e7-5c21-8c31-79b4eac65790" :answer/id #uuid "84cac5ce-e3e7-5c21-8c31-79b4eac65790" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-7,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9e8e1400-45eb-5e9a-b750-f95f072133d5" :answer/id #uuid "9e8e1400-45eb-5e9a-b750-f95f072133d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[-7,6]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e84fe7fd-6735-5887-8811-1577bf7dc94a" :answer/id #uuid "e84fe7fd-6735-5887-8811-1577bf7dc94a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{-7,-5,-3,-1,0,2,4,6\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-86108145-1c61-593e-9944-c48c2d3ee18a" :answer/id #uuid "86108145-1c61-593e-9944-c48c2d3ee18a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{-7,-5,-3,-1,0,4,6\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f0a977cc-2b1a-5047-8a3c-d6058da4b075" :answer/id #uuid "f0a977cc-2b1a-5047-8a3c-d6058da4b075" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{-7,0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083180 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-4ecf9c80-3378-55e5-9ee3-61d34805f6d4" "question-eb6a9a5f-89b9-5986-bd3d-889c98bdbbd7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-4ecf9c80-3378-55e5-9ee3-61d34805f6d4" :question/id #uuid "4ecf9c80-3378-55e5-9ee3-61d34805f6d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-129333" :question/problem "![](images/57/579e17e56674e39e552f1c0856f40e7f878ed94248a7a0e878c1f851c54ecbea.png)\n\nWhat is the range of the function $f(x),$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the lowest and highest $y$-values in the graph.\n\n- The lowest $y$-value is $-3.$ This occurs at the point $(3,-3).$\n\n- The highest $y$-value is $1.$ This occurs at the point $(-1,1).$\n\nThe function covers all the $y$-values between $-3$ and $1,$ including both $-3$ and $1.$\n\nTherefore, the range is $-3\\le y\\le 1,$ which can also be written as  $-3\\le f(x)\\le 1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b8128f7f-f2e6-5c3a-88a9-33f221275500"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b8128f7f-f2e6-5c3a-88a9-33f221275500" :answer-field/id #uuid "b8128f7f-f2e6-5c3a-88a9-33f221275500" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-188c4fda-9403-5e96-8778-6fa47508ca07" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a548bfd7-7287-5be4-92d7-196f40aaeb6b" "answer-31e170db-9a48-588a-8a1d-9fbc906b510e" "answer-8837b46e-1a4c-5bec-be6d-a7dbe8b25314" "answer-188c4fda-9403-5e96-8778-6fa47508ca07" "answer-d4b92c31-a6c4-51c9-9ea1-65459509653c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a548bfd7-7287-5be4-92d7-196f40aaeb6b" :answer/id #uuid "a548bfd7-7287-5be4-92d7-196f40aaeb6b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1\\le f(x)\\le 3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-31e170db-9a48-588a-8a1d-9fbc906b510e" :answer/id #uuid "31e170db-9a48-588a-8a1d-9fbc906b510e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3\\le f(x)\\le -1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8837b46e-1a4c-5bec-be6d-a7dbe8b25314" :answer/id #uuid "8837b46e-1a4c-5bec-be6d-a7dbe8b25314" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3\\le f(x)\\le 0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-188c4fda-9403-5e96-8778-6fa47508ca07" :answer/id #uuid "188c4fda-9403-5e96-8778-6fa47508ca07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3\\le f(x)\\le 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d4b92c31-a6c4-51c9-9ea1-65459509653c" :answer/id #uuid "d4b92c31-a6c4-51c9-9ea1-65459509653c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\le f(x)\\le 3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-eb6a9a5f-89b9-5986-bd3d-889c98bdbbd7" :question/id #uuid "eb6a9a5f-89b9-5986-bd3d-889c98bdbbd7" :question/math-academy-id "q-223598" :question/problem "![](images/e8/e874f46cd9a95c8bff5316128c72f4fd216194e44f54dc0929f6ad53a2e6a4c9.png)\n\nWhat is the range of the function $f(x),$ shown above?\n\n{{field-1}}\n$<\\,f(x)$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the lowest and highest $y$-values in the graph.\n\n- The lowest $y$-value is $-4.$ This occurs at the point $(-4,-4).$ However note that this point is not actually included in the graph.\n\n- The highest $y$-value is $5.$ This occurs at the point $(4,5).$\n\nThe function covers all the $y$-values between $-4$ and $5,$ including $5$ but not including $-4.$\n\nTherefore, the range is $-4<y\\le 5,$ which can also be written as $-4<f(x)\\le 5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-75b2a0de-fa1b-52ac-9b84-916e78eff091" "answer-field-47d5073b-231a-54ee-a7b5-cd502b4cbda6" "answer-field-959adb46-231a-5540-9f7d-05d88f3e81fe"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-75b2a0de-fa1b-52ac-9b84-916e78eff091" :answer-field/id #uuid "75b2a0de-fa1b-52ac-9b84-916e78eff091" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/