\n\nWe are also told that of those participants, $25%$ preferred landscapes. So, the number of participants who preferred landscape painting is\n\n$$\n0.25(0.6x)=0.15x.\n$$\n\nThe expression $0.15x$ represents $15%$ of $x.$ Therefore, $15%$ of all participants preferred landscape painting." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8c5934ba-d051-5992-8338-41334a774b4f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8c5934ba-d051-5992-8338-41334a774b4f" :answer-field/id #uuid "8c5934ba-d051-5992-8338-41334a774b4f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e420f7a2-62fb-57ef-956f-b0875cfcffa9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e420f7a2-62fb-57ef-956f-b0875cfcffa9" "answer-c8f27be0-083f-5731-b1fd-e01f4f406ebf" "answer-d6e51400-072c-5b9e-8e97-35b9e1b59817" "answer-6e949d25-1381-5079-b809-094d27a97f04" "answer-b199cd17-c18e-5be7-a027-a7f522f133b0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e420f7a2-62fb-57ef-956f-b0875cfcffa9" :answer/id #uuid "e420f7a2-62fb-57ef-956f-b0875cfcffa9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c8f27be0-083f-5731-b1fd-e01f4f406ebf" :answer/id #uuid "c8f27be0-083f-5731-b1fd-e01f4f406ebf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d6e51400-072c-5b9e-8e97-35b9e1b59817" :answer/id #uuid "d6e51400-072c-5b9e-8e97-35b9e1b59817" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e949d25-1381-5079-b809-094d27a97f04" :answer/id #uuid "6e949d25-1381-5079-b809-094d27a97f04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b199cd17-c18e-5be7-a027-a7f522f133b0" :answer/id #uuid "b199cd17-c18e-5be7-a027-a7f522f133b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "45%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-61eb5e2e-fcaa-52d1-ac70-97110690d4d7" :question/id #uuid "61eb5e2e-fcaa-52d1-ac70-97110690d4d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-326465" :question/problem "According to a recent report, $60%$ of tablet owners said they used their tablets regularly. Of those, $50%$ said they used them primarily for drawing. What percentage of all tablet owners used tablets primarily for drawing?" :question/worked-solution "Let $x$ be the total number of tablet owners.\n\nWe're told that $60%$ of tablet owners used their tablets regularly. Thus, the number of tablet owners who use them regularly is $0.6x.$\n\nWe are also told that of those owners, $50%$ used them for drawing. So, the number of tablet owners who used tablets primarily for drawing is\n\n$$\n0.50(0.6x)=0.30x.\n$$\n\nThe expression $0.30x$ represents $30%$ of $x.$ Therefore, $30%$ of all tablet owners used tablets primarily for drawing." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2eb59fef-3913-52e0-b381-93b8afe722d4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2eb59fef-3913-52e0-b381-93b8afe722d4" :answer-field/id #uuid "2eb59fef-3913-52e0-b381-93b8afe722d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4be72f5e-d8f1-550b-b61f-4fa75e6788eb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4be72f5e-d8f1-550b-b61f-4fa75e6788eb" "answer-260423ca-c450-564c-9729-9051afdbdb30" "answer-a33ca1d2-8570-5b69-8b96-022db448b553" "answer-e2fbfada-c622-57dd-ad25-59b2dadc7979" "answer-e81179df-8a40-5429-9632-3ec632cd68d9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4be72f5e-d8f1-550b-b61f-4fa75e6788eb" :answer/id #uuid "4be72f5e-d8f1-550b-b61f-4fa75e6788eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-260423ca-c450-564c-9729-9051afdbdb30" :answer/id #uuid "260423ca-c450-564c-9729-9051afdbdb30" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "35%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a33ca1d2-8570-5b69-8b96-022db448b553" :answer/id #uuid "a33ca1d2-8570-5b69-8b96-022db448b553" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "40%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e2fbfada-c622-57dd-ad25-59b2dadc7979" :answer/id #uuid "e2fbfada-c622-57dd-ad25-59b2dadc7979" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "50%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e81179df-8a40-5429-9632-3ec632cd68d9" :answer/id #uuid "e81179df-8a40-5429-9632-3ec632cd68d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "60%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186229194 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0a83854e-3aa1-59c0-86af-4b09c747a5fc" "question-ce7e59b5-3648-5abc-999d-9cb3832d5475"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186229609 :question/problem "A store marked up the price of a jacket to $150%$ of its original cost. The tax on the jacket is $30%$ of its marked-up price.\nIf the jacket originally cost $$60,$ what is the tax on the jacket?\n\nThe tax on the jacket is $$$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, the marked-up price is $150%$ of the original cost $($60):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}150%\\times 60 & =\\frac{150}{100}\\times 60 \\\\  & =1.5\\times 60 \\\\  & =90\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the marked-up price of the jacket is $$90.$\nThen, the tax is $30%$ of this price:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}30%\\times 90 & =\\frac{30}{100}\\times 90 \\\\  & =0.3\\times 90 \\\\  & =27\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tax on the jacket is $$27.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186227997 :answer-field/correct "answer-be31978a-e66c-5914-a793-35965a56b7fc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-be31978a-e66c-5914-a793-35965a56b7fc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-be31978a-e66c-5914-a793-35965a56b7fc" :answer/id #uuid "be31978a-e66c-5914-a793-35965a56b7fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-0a83854e-3aa1-59c0-86af-4b09c747a5fc" :question/id #uuid "0a83854e-3aa1-59c0-86af-4b09c747a5fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-327532" :question/problem "A chemist increased the concentration of a lab solution to $125%$ of its original level. An additional reagent then increased that new concentration by $20%.$ If the original concentration was $80$ units, how many additional units were added solely by the reagent?\n\nThe reagent added \n{{field-1}}\nadditional units to the concentration." :question/worked-solution "First, the new concentration is $125%$ of the original $(80$ units$):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}125%\\times 80 & =\\frac{125}{100}\\times 80 \\\\  & =1.25\\times 80 \\\\  & =100\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the new concentration is $100$ units. Then, the increase due to the reagent is $20%$ of this amount:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20%\\times 100 & =\\frac{20}{100}\\times 100 \\\\  & =0.2\\times 100 \\\\  & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the reagent added $20$ additional units to the concentration." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7a897728-e4f7-5404-b951-a57ef68ace56"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7a897728-e4f7-5404-b951-a57ef68ace56" :answer-field/id #uuid "7a897728-e4f7-5404-b951-a57ef68ace56" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-0d814d78-c63a-5ab2-ad13-3b9219c8d97c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0d814d78-c63a-5ab2-ad13-3b9219c8d97c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d814d78-c63a-5ab2-ad13-3b9219c8d97c" :answer/id #uuid "0d814d78-c63a-5ab2-ad13-3b9219c8d97c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ce7e59b5-3648-5abc-999d-9cb3832d5475" :question/id #uuid "ce7e59b5-3648-5abc-999d-9cb3832d5475" :question/math-academy-id "q-327544" :question/problem "An event organizer raised a ticket’s price to $160%$ of its original cost. A tax of $10%$ was applied to the marked-up price. If the ticket originally cost $$75,$ what is the tax?\n\nThe tax on the ticket is $$$  \n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, the marked-up price is $160%$ of the original cost $($75):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}160%\\times 75 & =\\frac{160}{100}\\times 75 \\\\  & =1.6\\times 75 \\\\  & =120\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the marked-up price of the ticket is $$120.$ Then, the tax is $10%$ of this price:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10%\\times 120 & =\\frac{10}{100}\\times 120 \\\\  & =0.1\\times 120 \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tax on the ticket is $$12.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6d38fd3a-1929-5eb8-b057-98cae4f07a49"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6d38fd3a-1929-5eb8-b057-98cae4f07a49" :answer-field/id #uuid "6d38fd3a-1929-5eb8-b057-98cae4f07a49" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-cd4fe015-c4ea-5dd1-9dd5-eccb94b29510" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cd4fe015-c4ea-5dd1-9dd5-eccb94b29510"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cd4fe015-c4ea-5dd1-9dd5-eccb94b29510" :answer/id #uuid "cd4fe015-c4ea-5dd1-9dd5-eccb94b29510" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-c74fe8fe-ab17-5021-aa6e-cba45f79c1ff" :activity/id #uuid "c74fe8fe-ab17-5021-aa6e-cba45f79c1ff" :activity/title "Applying Percentages in Succession" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050625 :activity/course 17592186046648 :activity/steps ["step-e843ada6-b68d-519e-b765-5a7d5f01b61e" "step-c1786767-df2d-5dac-97ac-8e1b734195a6" "step-9110eb6a-2e93-51c7-a5d3-f3d5f6f274b2" "step-2953197d-53f0-53b5-ae5a-55d33ffe4638" "step-350b7139-1fab-56d4-86bf-e150f9c15fcd"] :activity/first-step "step-e843ada6-b68d-519e-b765-5a7d5f01b61e" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-e843ada6-b68d-519e-b765-5a7d5f01b61e" :step/id #uuid "e843ada6-b68d-519e-b765-5a7d5f01b61e" :step/content "question-f7253d28-4651-534c-8fab-305435de6a5d" :step/next "step-c1786767-df2d-5dac-97ac-8e1b734195a6" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c1786767-df2d-5dac-97ac-8e1b734195a6" :step/id #uuid "c1786767-df2d-5dac-97ac-8e1b734195a6" :step/content "question-61eb5e2e-fcaa-52d1-ac70-97110690d4d7" :step/next "step-9110eb6a-2e93-51c7-a5d3-f3d5f6f274b2" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-9110eb6a-2e93-51c7-a5d3-f3d5f6f274b2" :step/id #uuid "9110eb6a-2e93-51c7-a5d3-f3d5f6f274b2" :step/content 17592186229609 :step/next "step-2953197d-53f0-53b5-ae5a-55d33ffe4638" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-2953197d-53f0-53b5-ae5a-55d33ffe4638" :step/id #uuid "2953197d-53f0-53b5-ae5a-55d33ffe4638" :step/content "question-0a83854e-3aa1-59c0-86af-4b09c747a5fc" :step/next "step-350b7139-1fab-56d4-86bf-e150f9c15fcd" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-350b7139-1fab-56d4-86bf-e150f9c15fcd" :step/id #uuid "350b7139-1fab-56d4-86bf-e150f9c15fcd" :step/content "question-ce7e59b5-3648-5abc-999d-9cb3832d5475" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186177135 :answer-field/choices 17592186177136] [:db/retract 17592186177135 :answer-field/choices 17592186177138] [:db/retract 17592186177135 :answer-field/choices 17592186177139] [:db/retract 17592186177135 :answer-field/choices 17592186177140] {:db/id 17592186179689 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c8edc0c0-9a3d-5546-8149-aa1e5f0446b7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179691 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f311fcaa-7f7c-50da-9066-652f1bc7fb5e" "question-69db9a7c-5652-51d3-8060-5596c178f982" "question-2c76b758-88c8-5667-93d2-dbb6a9e1da40"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179911 :question/problem "Calculate $∇\\times (F-G)$ at the point $(-2,0,3)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=z{e}^{y}\\,i+3\\,j-x\\,k,\\,(∇\\times G)(x,y,z)=2x{e}^{y}\\,i-2{e}^{y}\\,j.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $∇\\times (kF)=k∇\\times F$\n\n- $∇\\times (F+G)=∇\\times F+∇\\times G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F-G) & =∇\\times F-∇\\times G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\times F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ z{e}^{y} & 3 & -x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-x)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(3)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-x)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(z{e}^{y})]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(z{e}^{y})]k \\\\  & =(0-0)i-((-1)-{e}^{y})j+(0-z{e}^{y})k \\\\  & =({e}^{y}+1)\\,j-z{e}^{y}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F-G) & =∇\\times F-∇\\times G \\\\  & =({e}^{y}+1)\\,j-z{e}^{y}\\,k-[2x{e}^{y}\\,i-2{e}^{y}\\,j] \\\\  & =({e}^{y}+1)\\,j-z{e}^{y}\\,k-2x{e}^{y}\\,i+2{e}^{y}\\,j \\\\  & =-2x{e}^{y}\\,i+(3{e}^{y}+1)\\,j-z{e}^{y}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(-2,0,3),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(∇\\times (F-G))(-2,0,3) & =-2(-2){e}^{0}\\,i+(3{e}^{0}+1)\\,j-3{e}^{0}\\,k \\\\  & =4\\,i+4\\,j-3\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186177135 :answer-field/correct "answer-d2f59412-f61c-5a93-9b03-097a20b5443f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-08afb4e5-f12f-5c39-8a4d-af1df6ce9745" "answer-5c3feea7-809e-5194-b77d-2a337acc1747" "answer-d2f59412-f61c-5a93-9b03-097a20b5443f" "answer-79d18dc1-c0bb-50e7-a72e-25cf91922adb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-08afb4e5-f12f-5c39-8a4d-af1df6ce9745" :answer/id #uuid "08afb4e5-f12f-5c39-8a4d-af1df6ce9745" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\,i-5\\,j+k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5c3feea7-809e-5194-b77d-2a337acc1747" :answer/id #uuid "5c3feea7-809e-5194-b77d-2a337acc1747" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,i+3\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d2f59412-f61c-5a93-9b03-097a20b5443f" :answer/id #uuid "d2f59412-f61c-5a93-9b03-097a20b5443f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\,i+4\\,j-3\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-79d18dc1-c0bb-50e7-a72e-25cf91922adb" :answer/id #uuid "79d18dc1-c0bb-50e7-a72e-25cf91922adb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\,j-2\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c8edc0c0-9a3d-5546-8149-aa1e5f0446b7" :question/id #uuid "c8edc0c0-9a3d-5546-8149-aa1e5f0446b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-105791" :question/problem "Calculate $∇\\times (4F+G)$ at the point $(0,1,-1)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=y{e}^{x}\\,i+xz\\,j+(y-1)\\,\\text{k},\\,(∇\\times G)(x,y,z)=z\\,i.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $∇\\times (kF)=k∇\\times F$\n\n- $∇\\times (F+G)=∇\\times F+∇\\times G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (4F+G) & =∇\\times (4F)+∇\\times G \\\\  & =4∇\\times F+∇\\times G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\times F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ y{e}^{x} & xz & y-1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y-1)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xz)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y-1)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(y{e}^{x})]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xz)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y{e}^{x})]k \\\\  & =(1-x)\\,i-(0-0)\\,j+(z-{e}^{x})\\,k \\\\  & =(1-x)\\,i+(z-{e}^{x})\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (4F+G) & =4(∇\\times F)+∇\\times G \\\\  & =4[(1-x)\\,i+(z-{e}^{x})\\,k]+z\\,i \\\\  & =4(1-x)\\,i+4(z-{e}^{x})\\,k+z\\,i \\\\  & =[4(1-x)+z]\\,i+4(z-{e}^{x})\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(0,1,-1),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(∇\\times (4F+G))(0,1,-1) & =[4(1-0)+(-1)]\\,i+4(-1-{e}^{0})\\,k \\\\  & =[4-1]\\,i+4(-1-1)\\,k \\\\  & =3\\,i-8\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a2e1827e-bb95-5b76-9c80-da8e23a83f9e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a2e1827e-bb95-5b76-9c80-da8e23a83f9e" :answer-field/id #uuid "a2e1827e-bb95-5b76-9c80-da8e23a83f9e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-58ec558c-d6f3-58e0-9b30-c9079a8514c0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c21e913d-8c60-59fd-a2f7-ee60ea0be642" "answer-22b1f7e6-4442-5e2a-a841-c7b32ae47e40" "answer-94698b03-5cff-5cf9-93a7-70a660e8ea1d" "answer-58ec558c-d6f3-58e0-9b30-c9079a8514c0" "answer-d05504c9-446a-5857-96c3-6d98b995534b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c21e913d-8c60-59fd-a2f7-ee60ea0be642" :answer/id #uuid "c21e913d-8c60-59fd-a2f7-ee60ea0be642" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-22b1f7e6-4442-5e2a-a841-c7b32ae47e40" :answer/id #uuid "22b1f7e6-4442-5e2a-a841-c7b32ae47e40" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-i" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-94698b03-5cff-5cf9-93a7-70a660e8ea1d" :answer/id #uuid "94698b03-5cff-5cf9-93a7-70a660e8ea1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,j+5\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-58ec558c-d6f3-58e0-9b30-c9079a8514c0" :answer/id #uuid "58ec558c-d6f3-58e0-9b30-c9079a8514c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,i-8\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d05504c9-446a-5857-96c3-6d98b995534b" :answer/id #uuid "d05504c9-446a-5857-96c3-6d98b995534b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f311fcaa-7f7c-50da-9066-652f1bc7fb5e" :question/id #uuid "f311fcaa-7f7c-50da-9066-652f1bc7fb5e" :question/math-academy-id "q-105897" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨x{e}^{y},z,0⟩$ and the scalar field $f(x,y,z)=x-{e}^{y}.$ Given that\n\n$$\n∇\\times F=⟨-1,0,-x{e}^{y}⟩,\\,∇f=⟨1,-{e}^{y},0⟩,\n$$\n\ncalculate $∇\\times (f\\,F)$ at the point $(2,0,-3).$" :question/worked-solution "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\times (f\\,F)=f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇f\\times F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -{e}^{y} & 0 \\\\ x{e}^{y} & z & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[-{e}^{y}(0)-0(z)]i-[1(0)-0(x{e}^{y})]j+[1(z)-(-{e}^{y})(x{e}^{y})]k \\\\  & =0\\,i-0\\,j+(z+x{e}^{2y})\\,k \\\\  & =⟨0,0,z+x{e}^{2y}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F) & =f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F \\\\  & =(x-{e}^{y})⟨-1,0,-x{e}^{y}⟩+⟨0,0,z+x{e}^{2y}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{y}-x,0,x{e}^{2y}-{x}^{2}{e}^{y}⟩+⟨0,0,z+x{e}^{2y}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{y}-x,0,2x{e}^{2y}+z-{x}^{2}{e}^{y}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F)(2,0,-3) & =⟨{e}^{0}-2,0,2(2){e}^{2(0)}+(-3)-(2)^{2}{e}^{0}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-87266618-2882-52b8-96d1-51f6b11cd2c6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-87266618-2882-52b8-96d1-51f6b11cd2c6" :answer-field/id #uuid "87266618-2882-52b8-96d1-51f6b11cd2c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-675820df-6ea9-5f30-9192-0ae8291264b1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-675820df-6ea9-5f30-9192-0ae8291264b1" "answer-d9d9f5c3-101a-532e-8e93-6d12cddd64ee" "answer-c6a645d3-a518-5b55-bd59-e07fe9e39994" "answer-067e0099-a214-57d4-869c-c70c94a82c32" "answer-6aa35d43-0a5c-5368-b9f4-e38bbe3647e2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-675820df-6ea9-5f30-9192-0ae8291264b1" :answer/id #uuid "675820df-6ea9-5f30-9192-0ae8291264b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-1,0,-3⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d9d9f5c3-101a-532e-8e93-6d12cddd64ee" :answer/id #uuid "d9d9f5c3-101a-532e-8e93-6d12cddd64ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,0,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c6a645d3-a518-5b55-bd59-e07fe9e39994" :answer/id #uuid "c6a645d3-a518-5b55-bd59-e07fe9e39994" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,3,-2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-067e0099-a214-57d4-869c-c70c94a82c32" :answer/id #uuid "067e0099-a214-57d4-869c-c70c94a82c32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2,0,-3⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6aa35d43-0a5c-5368-b9f4-e38bbe3647e2" :answer/id #uuid "6aa35d43-0a5c-5368-b9f4-e38bbe3647e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨3,-2,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-69db9a7c-5652-51d3-8060-5596c178f982" :question/id #uuid "69db9a7c-5652-51d3-8060-5596c178f982" :question/math-academy-id "q-105958" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨0,{e}^{3x},2y⟩$ and the scalar field $f(x,y,z)=2x+3.$ Given that\n\n$$\n∇\\times F=⟨2,0,3{e}^{3x}⟩,\\,∇f=⟨2,0,0⟩,\n$$\n\ncalculate $∇\\times (f\\,F)$ at the point $(0,-1,4).$" :question/worked-solution "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\times (f\\,F)=f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇f\\times F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3x} & 2y\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[0(2y)-0({e}^{3x})]i-[2(2y)-0(0)]j+[2({e}^{3x})-0(0)]k \\\\  & =0\\,i-4y\\,j+2{e}^{3x}\\,k \\\\  & =⟨0,-4y,2{e}^{3x}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F) & =f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F \\\\  & =(2x+3)⟨2,0,3{e}^{3x}⟩+⟨0,-4y,2{e}^{3x}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2(2x+3),0,(6x+9){e}^{3x}⟩+⟨0,-4y,2{e}^{3x}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2(2x+3),-4y,(6x+11){e}^{3x}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F)(0,-1,4) & =⟨2(2(0)+3),-4(-1),(6(0)+11){e}^{3(0)}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,4,11⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-36ec198d-cd51-504c-b007-6c8fdb361499"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-36ec198d-cd51-504c-b007-6c8fdb361499" :answer-field/id #uuid "36ec198d-cd51-504c-b007-6c8fdb361499" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c7002173-662f-590e-85c4-bebb1d460e6e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f00a9184-3171-5cc7-9fb6-e28f4ae84e39" "answer-543874d6-b5ec-5cf9-ad85-65e957697883" "answer-406d7fc1-59b5-57a2-93cd-988d48533d9e" "answer-c7002173-662f-590e-85c4-bebb1d460e6e" "answer-d35ebd08-4a97-5d01-9b27-dd8017794e01"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f00a9184-3171-5cc7-9fb6-e28f4ae84e39" :answer/id #uuid "f00a9184-3171-5cc7-9fb6-e28f4ae84e39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-3,0,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-543874d6-b5ec-5cf9-ad85-65e957697883" :answer/id #uuid "543874d6-b5ec-5cf9-ad85-65e957697883" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,-1,4⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-406d7fc1-59b5-57a2-93cd-988d48533d9e" :answer/id #uuid "406d7fc1-59b5-57a2-93cd-988d48533d9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,4,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c7002173-662f-590e-85c4-bebb1d460e6e" :answer/id #uuid "c7002173-662f-590e-85c4-bebb1d460e6e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨6,4,11⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d35ebd08-4a97-5d01-9b27-dd8017794e01" :answer/id #uuid "d35ebd08-4a97-5d01-9b27-dd8017794e01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨9,3,4⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2c76b758-88c8-5667-93d2-dbb6a9e1da40" :question/id #uuid "2c76b758-88c8-5667-93d2-dbb6a9e1da40" :question/math-academy-id "q-105956" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨z,\\sqrt{x},0⟩$ and the scalar field $f(x,y,z)=-z.$ Given that\n\n$$\n∇\\times F=⟨0,1,\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}⟩,\\,∇f=⟨0,0,-1⟩,\n$$\n\ncalculate $∇\\times (f\\,F)$ at the point $(4,1,4).$" :question/worked-solution "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\times (f\\,F)=f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇f\\times F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ z & \\sqrt{x} & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[0(0)-(-1)(\\sqrt{x})]i-[0(0)-(-1)(z)]j+[0(\\sqrt{x})-0(z)]k \\\\  & =\\sqrt{x}\\,i-z\\,j+0\\,k \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{x},-z,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F) & =f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F \\\\  & =(-z)⟨0,1,\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}⟩+⟨\\sqrt{x},-z,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-z,-\\frac{z}{2\\sqrt{x}}⟩+⟨\\sqrt{x},-z,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{x},-2z,-\\frac{z}{2\\sqrt{x}}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F)(4,1,4) & =⟨\\sqrt{4},-2(4),-\\frac{4}{2\\sqrt{4}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-8,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cee411fe-3c0d-5c7d-9c42-5d9b1df29d7b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cee411fe-3c0d-5c7d-9c42-5d9b1df29d7b" :answer-field/id #uuid "cee411fe-3c0d-5c7d-9c42-5d9b1df29d7b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3e626866-926c-5638-8514-10fe8911bfb9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ce34e2bd-fa56-525d-9e23-0ce1549d6ea8" "answer-62f0f666-5714-5bdd-ac2c-a5c2b0a1ad02" "answer-1dcb20c5-ace4-5356-918e-a260adfc5b75" "answer-67b3423e-e4b7-56ef-b64b-3bde9aa959ef" "answer-3e626866-926c-5638-8514-10fe8911bfb9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ce34e2bd-fa56-525d-9e23-0ce1549d6ea8" :answer/id #uuid "ce34e2bd-fa56-525d-9e23-0ce1549d6ea8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-2,4,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-62f0f666-5714-5bdd-ac2c-a5c2b0a1ad02" :answer/id #uuid "62f0f666-5714-5bdd-ac2c-a5c2b0a1ad02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-4,-1,-4⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1dcb20c5-ace4-5356-918e-a260adfc5b75" :answer/id #uuid "1dcb20c5-ace4-5356-918e-a260adfc5b75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-4,1,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-67b3423e-e4b7-56ef-b64b-3bde9aa959ef" :answer/id #uuid "67b3423e-e4b7-56ef-b64b-3bde9aa959ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨1,4,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3e626866-926c-5638-8514-10fe8911bfb9" :answer/id #uuid "3e626866-926c-5638-8514-10fe8911bfb9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2,-8,-1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186180687 :tutorial/content "Recall that if $\\mathbf F = P\\,\\mathbf i + Q\\,\\mathbf j + R\\,\\mathbf k$ is a vector field on $\\mathbb R^3,$ then the curl of $\\mathbf F$ is given by\n\n![](images/ce/ce53aa0d141921708855b14deda9363d69788fd9525bdcbc4426d887aa4d0f70.svg)\n\nThe curl is a quantity that's made up of derivatives, so we would expect it to have similar properties to derivatives.\n\nFor example, if $\\mathbf F$ and $\\mathbf H$ are vector fields and $k$ is a scalar constant, then we have the following linearity properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∇\\times (kF)=k\\,∇\\times F \\\\  & ∇\\times (F+G)=∇\\times F+∇\\times G\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying these rules can often help us to save time when computing curl. Let's see some examples." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179854 :activity/expected-seconds 720.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "knowledge-point-9f161693-0317-5b9e-9156-c781f703a4c0" :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f161693-0317-5b9e-9156-c781f703a4c0" :knowledge-point/canonical-example "question-11a8381c-60e6-54f2-ac78-bece2edc403e" :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ee55fb2d-2168-5fe7-9d4c-8b219d79c6ed" "question-3e99cefe-dda5-5d51-81b5-68b7b4241052" "question-40ca59d6-4e89-5334-bddb-bed9c8ab1c58" "question-63a4febd-402b-590e-88f3-6d9132bd98e1"] :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Number as a Finite Decimal Using Long Division" :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186408188 :topic/knowledge-points ["knowledge-point-9f161693-0317-5b9e-9156-c781f703a4c0" "knowledge-point-2ee93f86-38d1-591a-b694-a4f455240d75" "knowledge-point-4c28dcab-dd12-58c2-88c6-0301dc0f9ce4" "knowledge-point-9f161693-0317-5b9e-9156-c781f703a4c0" "knowledge-point-9f161693-0317-5b9e-9156-c781f703a4c0" "knowledge-point-9f161693-0317-5b9e-9156-c781f703a4c0" "knowledge-point-9f161693-0317-5b9e-9156-c781f703a4c0" "knowledge-point-2ee93f86-38d1-591a-b694-a4f455240d75" "knowledge-point-2ee93f86-38d1-591a-b694-a4f455240d75" "knowledge-point-4c28dcab-dd12-58c2-88c6-0301dc0f9ce4" "knowledge-point-4c28dcab-dd12-58c2-88c6-0301dc0f9ce4"] :db/ensure [:topic/identity-validate]} {:db/id "question-11a8381c-60e6-54f2-ac78-bece2edc403e" :question/id #uuid "11a8381c-60e6-54f2-ac78-bece2edc403e" :question/math-academy-id "e-22733" :question/problem "Convert $\\dfrac{35}{4}$ into a decimal using long division." :question/worked-solution "To write the fraction as a decimal, we divide the numerator by the denominator:\n\n$$\n35 \\div 4\n$$\n\nWe proceed using long division as usual, stopping once we obtain a remainder of $0$:\n\n![](images/ad/adfe6e3eeef5940412a5231d0342dfbab55c3352145b5964ced86841c920590e.svg)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{35}{4} = 8.75.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "knowledge-point-2ee93f86-38d1-591a-b694-a4f455240d75" :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ee93f86-38d1-591a-b694-a4f455240d75" :knowledge-point/canonical-example "question-2953724f-e9c5-5a58-a253-c1d894297cc0" :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e7f88181-a4ac-5313-9245-814758011d78" "question-2e203a6d-9350-554f-8fa6-0f2ee030fe0b"] :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Number as a Repeating Decimal Using Long Division" :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-2953724f-e9c5-5a58-a253-c1d894297cc0" :question/id #uuid "2953724f-e9c5-5a58-a253-c1d894297cc0" :question/math-academy-id "e-22734" :question/problem "Convert $\\dfrac{79}{6}$ into a repeated decimal using long division." :question/worked-solution "To write the fraction as a decimal, we divide the numerator by the denominator:\n\n$$\n79 \\div 6\n$$\n\nWe proceed using long division as usual, continuing until a repeating pattern of digits appears after the decimal point:\n\n![](images/3c/3c9add129b16a1dedeb68e0397f6345d7f481f3bbfdd54c0a35067abaaa15263.svg)\n\nWe could continue the division, but the same digit keeps repeating. Thus, the decimal continues with repeating $6$'s:\n\n$$\n13.16\\ldots\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{79}{6} = 13.16\\ldots = 13.1\\overline{6}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "knowledge-point-4c28dcab-dd12-58c2-88c6-0301dc0f9ce4" :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c28dcab-dd12-58c2-88c6-0301dc0f9ce4" :knowledge-point/canonical-example "question-975545b6-bff4-5fab-aaf4-e8ee01507788" :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5f502aa5-65d4-518a-a479-69aa4507aee1" 17592186152676] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Rational Decimals" :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-975545b6-bff4-5fab-aaf4-e8ee01507788" :question/id #uuid "975545b6-bff4-5fab-aaf4-e8ee01507788" :question/math-academy-id "e-22727" :question/problem "Which of the following numbers are rational?\n\nI. $1.577$\n\nII. $8.163452 \\ldots$\n\nIII. $2.\\overline{73}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of our numbers in turn.\n\n- $1.577$ is a rational number because it can be expressed as a ratio of two integers:\n\n$$\n1.577 = \\dfrac{1\\,577}{1\\,000}\n$$\n\n- $8.163452 \\ldots$ is not a rational number. The notation \"$\\ldots$\" tells us that digits after the decimal point extend forever. Because there is no indicated repeating pattern, this represents a non-terminating, non-repeating decimal.\n\n- $2.\\overline{73}$ is a rational number. The notation $\\overline{73}$ tells us that the digits $7$ and $3$ after the decimal point repeat indefinitely.\n\n$$\n2.\\overline{73} = 2.73737373\\ldots\n$$\n\nAny decimal with repeating digits can be represented as a ratio of two integers. In this case,\n\n$$\n2.\\overline{73}  = \\dfrac{271}{99}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-ee55fb2d-2168-5fe7-9d4c-8b219d79c6ed" :question/id #uuid "ee55fb2d-2168-5fe7-9d4c-8b219d79c6ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-357330" :question/problem "Convert $\\frac{17}{8}$ into a decimal using long division." :question/worked-solution "To write down the given fraction as a decimal, we need to divide the numerator by the denominator:\n\n$$\n17÷8\n$$\n\nWe proceed using the long division as usual, stopping once we obtain a remainder of $0:$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"150\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"left\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"5\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,\\,\\,2\\,.\\,1\\,2\\,5$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$8$</td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"5\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{1\\,\\phantom{|}7\\,.\\,0\\,\\phantom{|}0\\,\\phantom{|}0}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$8$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$6$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{17}{8}=2.125.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ae88c8ac-95f7-5200-b180-6af001020dfe"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ae88c8ac-95f7-5200-b180-6af001020dfe" :answer-field/id #uuid "ae88c8ac-95f7-5200-b180-6af001020dfe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e407094b-a9ef-5ee9-bcdb-94c0c5ae4c0c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e407094b-a9ef-5ee9-bcdb-94c0c5ae4c0c" "answer-11feea40-5160-56af-ad40-07e554fbb357" "answer-6f4fee77-cc5f-5c32-92c1-5d9da6a5595e" "answer-cab7e5c7-e09b-56de-bfd0-7fce435a6db9" "answer-afe14d7c-15c3-5d86-b336-862ca7b208d3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e407094b-a9ef-5ee9-bcdb-94c0c5ae4c0c" :answer/id #uuid "e407094b-a9ef-5ee9-bcdb-94c0c5ae4c0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.125" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-11feea40-5160-56af-ad40-07e554fbb357" :answer/id #uuid "11feea40-5160-56af-ad40-07e554fbb357" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.135" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6f4fee77-cc5f-5c32-92c1-5d9da6a5595e" :answer/id #uuid "6f4fee77-cc5f-5c32-92c1-5d9da6a5595e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.175" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cab7e5c7-e09b-56de-bfd0-7fce435a6db9" :answer/id #uuid "cab7e5c7-e09b-56de-bfd0-7fce435a6db9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.215" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-afe14d7c-15c3-5d86-b336-862ca7b208d3" :answer/id #uuid "afe14d7c-15c3-5d86-b336-862ca7b208d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.125" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3e99cefe-dda5-5d51-81b5-68b7b4241052" :question/id #uuid "3e99cefe-dda5-5d51-81b5-68b7b4241052" :question/math-academy-id "q-357520" :question/problem "Convert $\\frac{238}{8}$ into a decimal using long division." :question/worked-solution "To write the fraction as a decimal, we divide the numerator by the denominator:\n\n$$\n238÷8\n$$\n\nWe proceed using long division as usual, stopping once we obtain a remainder of $0:$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"150\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"left\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"5\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,\\,\\,2\\,9\\,.\\,7\\,5$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$8$</td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"5\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{2\\,\\phantom{|}3\\,\\phantom{|}8\\,.\\,0\\,\\phantom{|}0}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$7$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$8$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$7$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n