on/worked-solution "First, we express the given information in terms of $Φ:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\le z) & =0.40 \\\\ Φ(z) & =0.40\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we are looking for the value of $z$ such that\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.40).\n$$\n\nWe look for the column in the table that corresponds to $p=0.40,$ and we find that\n\n$$\np=0.40\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(p)=-0.2533.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.40)=-0.2533.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6e05090a-954b-5985-81a1-91310ca48f77"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6e05090a-954b-5985-81a1-91310ca48f77" :answer-field/id #uuid "6e05090a-954b-5985-81a1-91310ca48f77" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-9546136f-9e31-5ec3-bbbd-32bc3c2578d0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9546136f-9e31-5ec3-bbbd-32bc3c2578d0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9546136f-9e31-5ec3-bbbd-32bc3c2578d0" :answer/id #uuid "9546136f-9e31-5ec3-bbbd-32bc3c2578d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.2533" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d124118c-140f-52f2-b4ac-16dbd784c35b" :question/id #uuid "d124118c-140f-52f2-b4ac-16dbd784c35b" :question/math-academy-id "q-96933" :question/problem "The table below gives the values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.995.$\n\n| $p$ | $\\,0.900\\,$ | $\\,0.950\\,$ | $\\,0.975\\,$ | $\\,0.990\\,$ | $\\,0.995\\,$ | $\\,0.999\\,$ | $\\,0.9995\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ | $\\,1.9600\\,$ | $\\,2.3263\\,$ | $\\,2.5758\\,$ | $\\,3.0902\\,$ | $\\,3.2905\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, we express the given information in terms of $Φ:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\le z) & =0.995 \\\\ Φ(z) & =0.995\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we are looking for the value of $z$ such that\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.995).\n$$\n\nWe look for the column in the table that corresponds to $p=0.995,$ and we find that\n\n$$\np=0.995\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(p)=2.5758.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.995)=2.5758.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4fe11fc7-6fbb-5dee-bf1e-d62730e9a509"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4fe11fc7-6fbb-5dee-bf1e-d62730e9a509" :answer-field/id #uuid "4fe11fc7-6fbb-5dee-bf1e-d62730e9a509" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-907f9238-2918-58cd-9a06-3b899ae2f9e8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2ec30051-b0f4-5569-896b-0881dc28eda4" "answer-d4fd2043-1fad-56f6-912c-e1d9568bb630" "answer-ae1660cd-36d2-5645-8a6f-328abac9e59b" "answer-907f9238-2918-58cd-9a06-3b899ae2f9e8" "answer-e63d4436-06b2-5794-a1a0-a90f532c1812"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2ec30051-b0f4-5569-896b-0881dc28eda4" :answer/id #uuid "2ec30051-b0f4-5569-896b-0881dc28eda4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.6449" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d4fd2043-1fad-56f6-912c-e1d9568bb630" :answer/id #uuid "d4fd2043-1fad-56f6-912c-e1d9568bb630" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.9600" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae1660cd-36d2-5645-8a6f-328abac9e59b" :answer/id #uuid "ae1660cd-36d2-5645-8a6f-328abac9e59b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.3263" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-907f9238-2918-58cd-9a06-3b899ae2f9e8" :answer/id #uuid "907f9238-2918-58cd-9a06-3b899ae2f9e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.5758" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e63d4436-06b2-5794-a1a0-a90f532c1812" :answer/id #uuid "e63d4436-06b2-5794-a1a0-a90f532c1812" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.2905" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-498c3c25-8224-532d-867c-1bb7c9c3d797" :question/id #uuid "498c3c25-8224-532d-867c-1bb7c9c3d797" :question/math-academy-id "q-164331" :question/problem "The table below gives the values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.9995.$\n\n| $p$ | $\\,0.900\\,$ | $\\,0.950\\,$ | $\\,0.975\\,$ | $\\,0.990\\,$ | $\\,0.995\\,$ | $\\,0.999\\,$ | $\\,0.9995\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ | $\\,1.9600\\,$ | $\\,2.3263\\,$ | $\\,2.5758\\,$ | $\\,3.0902\\,$ | $\\,3.2905\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, we express the given information in terms of $Φ:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\le z) & =0.9995 \\\\ Φ(z) & =0.9995\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we are looking for the value of $z$ such that\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.9995).\n$$\n\nWe look for the column in the table that corresponds to $p=0.9995,$ and we find that\n\n$$\np=0.9995\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(p)=3.2905.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.9995)=3.2905.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-44c234c3-a395-5292-a122-e598d1b5e13a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-44c234c3-a395-5292-a122-e598d1b5e13a" :answer-field/id #uuid "44c234c3-a395-5292-a122-e598d1b5e13a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3adfc64b-e003-5630-aeb9-acf68f203a8d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ff819ae6-c0b0-5dab-9404-30f76f981bf4" "answer-69010aff-3ab9-5d0e-be44-6b0951a67112" "answer-20277f6b-6957-5eff-974f-9f54920b0c35" "answer-cd659ed7-8f4b-51cf-bea7-2ad403c7e94f" "answer-3adfc64b-e003-5630-aeb9-acf68f203a8d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff819ae6-c0b0-5dab-9404-30f76f981bf4" :answer/id #uuid "ff819ae6-c0b0-5dab-9404-30f76f981bf4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.5758" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-69010aff-3ab9-5d0e-be44-6b0951a67112" :answer/id #uuid "69010aff-3ab9-5d0e-be44-6b0951a67112" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.8330" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-20277f6b-6957-5eff-974f-9f54920b0c35" :answer/id #uuid "20277f6b-6957-5eff-974f-9f54920b0c35" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.0902" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cd659ed7-8f4b-51cf-bea7-2ad403c7e94f" :answer/id #uuid "cd659ed7-8f4b-51cf-bea7-2ad403c7e94f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.1903" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3adfc64b-e003-5630-aeb9-acf68f203a8d" :answer/id #uuid "3adfc64b-e003-5630-aeb9-acf68f203a8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.2905" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d5e93823-c39c-538e-930e-c856e7a48401" :question/id #uuid "d5e93823-c39c-538e-930e-c856e7a48401" :question/math-academy-id "q-328465" :question/problem "The table below gives the values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.20.$ Use the table below and do not round your answer.\n\n| $\\,p\\,$ | $0.10$ | $0.15$ | $0.20$ | $0.25$ | $0.30$ | $0.35$ | $0.40$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,-1.2816\\,$ | $\\,-1.0364\\,$ | $\\,-0.8416\\,$ | $\\,-0.6745\\,$ | $\\,-0.5244\\,$ | $\\,-0.3853\\,$ | $\\,-0.2533\\,$ |\n\n$z=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we express the given information in terms of $Φ:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\le z) & =0.20 \\\\ Φ(z) & =0.20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we are looking for the value of $z$ such that\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.20).\n$$\n\nWe look for the column in the table that corresponds to $p=0.20,$ and we find that\n\n$$\np=0.20\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(p)=-0.8416.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.20)=-0.8416.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-999a3746-3384-57c3-86de-e1e9693290b1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-999a3746-3384-57c3-86de-e1e9693290b1" :answer-field/id #uuid "999a3746-3384-57c3-86de-e1e9693290b1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-36c4c5da-0b79-53e8-b7d0-57bc45f85b0f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-36c4c5da-0b79-53e8-b7d0-57bc45f85b0f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-36c4c5da-0b79-53e8-b7d0-57bc45f85b0f" :answer/id #uuid "36c4c5da-0b79-53e8-b7d0-57bc45f85b0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.8416" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4d1937b2-4611-58ce-a050-d85b88c9c4df" :question/id #uuid "4d1937b2-4611-58ce-a050-d85b88c9c4df" :question/math-academy-id "q-164332" :question/problem "The table below gives the values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.10.$\n\n| $p$ | $\\,0.900\\,$ | $\\,0.950\\,$ | $\\,0.975\\,$ | $\\,0.990\\,$ | $\\,0.995\\,$ | $\\,0.999\\,$ | $\\,0.9995\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ | $\\,1.9600\\,$ | $\\,2.3263\\,$ | $\\,2.5758\\,$ | $\\,3.0902\\,$ | $\\,3.2905\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "From the table, notice that\n\n$$\nP(Z\\le 1.2816)=0.90.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(Z\\ge 1.2816)=1-0.90=0.10.\n$$\n\nBy the symmetry of the standard normal distribution, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(-1.2816)=0.10.\n$$\n\n![](images/fe/feb06180815c7ae83a5034ff8933700fd5778c9ab0bfba54fe95bb67104662b7.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-1.2816) & =0.10 \\\\ P(Z\\le -1.2816) & =0.10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required value of $z$ is $-1.2816.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-36d38cd0-7f8a-5483-a8b4-00b891bc2efd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-36d38cd0-7f8a-5483-a8b4-00b891bc2efd" :answer-field/id #uuid "36d38cd0-7f8a-5483-a8b4-00b891bc2efd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-64f67ed2-d6ad-582c-9058-5742f4394ed3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-64f67ed2-d6ad-582c-9058-5742f4394ed3" "answer-e9cee8aa-e3d3-56b7-97e8-19c302c5d275" "answer-6ff373d7-66ef-5f4e-85b7-ea2ef57bdfc7" "answer-e8a0e8c1-effb-5b17-a58a-5cba623c360a" "answer-95f8d5ee-929e-5317-8d0a-133e273ac264"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-64f67ed2-d6ad-582c-9058-5742f4394ed3" :answer/id #uuid "64f67ed2-d6ad-582c-9058-5742f4394ed3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.2816" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e9cee8aa-e3d3-56b7-97e8-19c302c5d275" :answer/id #uuid "e9cee8aa-e3d3-56b7-97e8-19c302c5d275" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.3263" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ff373d7-66ef-5f4e-85b7-ea2ef57bdfc7" :answer/id #uuid "6ff373d7-66ef-5f4e-85b7-ea2ef57bdfc7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3.0902" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8a0e8c1-effb-5b17-a58a-5cba623c360a" :answer/id #uuid "e8a0e8c1-effb-5b17-a58a-5cba623c360a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.2816" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-95f8d5ee-929e-5317-8d0a-133e273ac264" :answer/id #uuid "95f8d5ee-929e-5317-8d0a-133e273ac264" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.0902" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-222d3245-c08e-59e6-abe7-30dbec831345" :question/id #uuid "222d3245-c08e-59e6-abe7-30dbec831345" :question/math-academy-id "q-328480" :question/problem "The table below gives the values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z>z)=0.25.$ Use the table below and do not round your answer.\n\n| $\\,p\\,$ | $0.65$ | $0.70$ | $0.75$ | $0.80$ | $0.85$ | $0.90$ | $0.95$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,0.3853\\,$ | $\\,0.5244\\,$ | $\\,0.6745\\,$ | $\\,0.8416\\,$ | $\\,1.0364\\,$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ |\n\n$z=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we express the given information in terms of $Φ,$ using the complement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z>z) & =0.25 \\\\ 1-P(Z\\le z) & =0.25 \\\\ 1-Φ(z) & =0.25 \\\\ Φ(z) & =1-0.25 \\\\ Φ(z) & =0.75\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we are looking for the value of $z$ such that\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.75).\n$$\n\nWe look for the column in the table that corresponds to $p=0.75,$ and we find that\n\n$$\np=0.75\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(p)=0.6745.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.75)=0.6745.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-11eb93d2-4ed3-55c1-b04f-9715439b2be7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-11eb93d2-4ed3-55c1-b04f-9715439b2be7" :answer-field/id #uuid "11eb93d2-4ed3-55c1-b04f-9715439b2be7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-0c781b62-786a-5c02-b4cc-f00667fc5101" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0c781b62-786a-5c02-b4cc-f00667fc5101"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0c781b62-786a-5c02-b4cc-f00667fc5101" :answer/id #uuid "0c781b62-786a-5c02-b4cc-f00667fc5101" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.6745" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9ffb7646-1918-5230-b400-64576248fe40" :question/id #uuid "9ffb7646-1918-5230-b400-64576248fe40" :question/math-academy-id "q-328474" :question/problem "The table below gives the values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.025.$ Use the table below and do not round your answer.\n\n| $p$ | $\\,0.900\\,$ | $\\,0.950\\,$ | $\\,0.975\\,$ | $\\,0.990\\,$ | $\\,0.995\\,$ | $\\,0.999\\,$ | $\\,0.9995\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ | $\\,1.9600\\,$ | $\\,2.3263\\,$ | $\\,2.5758\\,$ | $\\,3.0902\\,$ | $\\,3.2905\\,$ |\n\n$z=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "From the table, notice that\n\n$$\nP(Z\\le 1.96)=0.975.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(Z\\ge 1.96)=1-0.975=0.025.\n$$\n\nBy the symmetry of the standard normal distribution, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(-1.96)=0.025.\n$$\n\n![](images/e4/e46e28a748745da14c260af2c39c7c10983b40476c57d8d75a51f0390d2359d2.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-1.96) & =0.025 \\\\ P(Z\\le -1.96) & =0.025.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required value of $z$ is $-1.96.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9bf92771-7c95-5c4e-a5e9-de264eeed978"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9bf92771-7c95-5c4e-a5e9-de264eeed978" :answer-field/id #uuid "9bf92771-7c95-5c4e-a5e9-de264eeed978" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-107b6af3-b6a7-5e28-a4ad-8e9b12ea92b3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-107b6af3-b6a7-5e28-a4ad-8e9b12ea92b3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-107b6af3-b6a7-5e28-a4ad-8e9b12ea92b3" :answer/id #uuid "107b6af3-b6a7-5e28-a4ad-8e9b12ea92b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.96" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e2cf6287-aa23-5f4b-8eb1-c626aabdf157" :question/id #uuid "e2cf6287-aa23-5f4b-8eb1-c626aabdf157" :question/math-academy-id "q-96960" :question/problem "The table below gives the values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.015.$\n\n| $\\,p\\,$ | $0.965$ | $0.970$ | $0.975$ | $0.980$ | $0.985$ | $0.990$ | $0.995$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,1.8119\\,$ | $\\,1.8808\\,$ | $\\,1.9600\\,$ | $\\,2.0537\\,$ | $\\,2.1701\\,$ | $\\,2.3263\\,$ | $\\,2.5758\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "From the table, notice that\n\n$$\nP(Z\\le 2.1701)=0.985.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(Z\\ge 2.1701)=1-0.985=0.015.\n$$\n\nBy the symmetry of the standard normal distribution, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(-2.1701)=0.015.\n$$\n\n![](images/47/47a123a730cf175bea1d1887ffdc5a9feb3e1d8f07208c28a9f893a9a1688005.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-2.1701) & =0.015 \\\\ P(Z\\le -2.1701) & =0.015.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required value of $z$ is $-2.1701.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9bebb073-a5c7-5042-9111-9520c6e6d7df"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9bebb073-a5c7-5042-9111-9520c6e6d7df" :answer-field/id #uuid "9bebb073-a5c7-5042-9111-9520c6e6d7df" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7a1947cb-f049-5278-8b27-3401af91bc08" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2a163fc6-b329-585d-a1b9-5b8e8a43d026" "answer-39268e53-d205-558c-a1f8-bd563702a8c7" "answer-7a1947cb-f049-5278-8b27-3401af91bc08" "answer-cc3e9a65-db77-574a-8530-080325a7bc3b" "answer-d1141597-71b6-58dd-a196-da185a8ff0b9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2a163fc6-b329-585d-a1b9-5b8e8a43d026" :answer/id #uuid "2a163fc6-b329-585d-a1b9-5b8e8a43d026" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.6449" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-39268e53-d205-558c-a1f8-bd563702a8c7" :answer/id #uuid "39268e53-d205-558c-a1f8-bd563702a8c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.9600" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7a1947cb-f049-5278-8b27-3401af91bc08" :answer/id #uuid "7a1947cb-f049-5278-8b27-3401af91bc08" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.1701" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cc3e9a65-db77-574a-8530-080325a7bc3b" :answer/id #uuid "cc3e9a65-db77-574a-8530-080325a7bc3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.8808" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d1141597-71b6-58dd-a196-da185a8ff0b9" :answer/id #uuid "d1141597-71b6-58dd-a196-da185a8ff0b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.5758" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166998 :activity/expected-seconds 540.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124451 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9d2fd7c0-6fec-5b30-98fe-3b0bf10ba9a4" "question-4a523061-b982-5542-a530-946bca7d0e33"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-9d2fd7c0-6fec-5b30-98fe-3b0bf10ba9a4" :question/id #uuid "9d2fd7c0-6fec-5b30-98fe-3b0bf10ba9a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-65338" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}.$ Find the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(2,4,4).$" :question/worked-solution "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b,c)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈f(a,b,c)+∇f(a,b,c)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b,z-c⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(2,4,4)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(2,4,4)+∇f(2,4,4)\\cdot ⟨x-2,y-4,z-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the definition of $f,$ we have that $f(2,4,4)=\\frac{1}{6}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x} & =-\\frac{x}{{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})}^{3/2}}\\,⇒\\,{f}_{x}(2,4,4)=-\\frac{2}{{({2}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{4}^{2})}^{3/2}}=-\\frac{1}{108}, \\\\ {f}_{y} & =-\\frac{y}{{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})}^{3/2}}\\,⇒\\,{f}_{y}(2,4,4)=-\\frac{4}{{({2}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{4}^{2})}^{3/2}}=-\\frac{1}{54}, \\\\ {f}_{z} & =-\\frac{z}{{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})}^{3/2}}\\,⇒\\,{f}_{z}(2,4,4)=-\\frac{4}{{({2}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{4}^{2})}^{3/2}}=-\\frac{1}{54}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient of the function at the point $(2,4,4)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(2,4,4) & =⟨{f}_{x}(2,4,4),{f}_{y}(2,4,4),{f}_{z}(2,4,4)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{108},-\\frac{1}{54},-\\frac{1}{54}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the linear approximation of the function $f$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(2,4,4)+∇f(2,4,4)\\cdot ⟨x-2,y-4,z-4⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}+⟨-\\frac{1}{108},-\\frac{1}{54},-\\frac{1}{54}⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,y-4,z-4⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{1}{108}(x-2)-\\frac{1}{54}(y-4)-\\frac{1}{54}(z-4) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{x}{108}+\\frac{1}{54}-\\frac{y}{54}+\\frac{4}{54}-\\frac{z}{54}+\\frac{4}{54} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{x}{108}-\\frac{y}{54}-\\frac{z}{54}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c5948ebf-b36f-50ef-996a-235488992a7d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c5948ebf-b36f-50ef-996a-235488992a7d" :answer-field/id #uuid "c5948ebf-b36f-50ef-996a-235488992a7d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4c8e5783-e729-5001-b425-9bd95d7f94c5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0f7d0aa5-2342-5d6f-a521-a62d6d54725c" "answer-52aebee7-a1be-5094-b50c-2fecab43978c" "answer-8b357635-83ca-53f3-be6f-efc2212bf65c" "answer-4c8e5783-e729-5001-b425-9bd95d7f94c5" "answer-bac0b568-47cf-5aed-a2d1-d6ae3ec5aafb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0f7d0aa5-2342-5d6f-a521-a62d6d54725c" :answer/id #uuid "0f7d0aa5-2342-5d6f-a521-a62d6d54725c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)≈-\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{x}{108}+\\frac{y}{54}+\\frac{z}{54}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-52aebee7-a1be-5094-b50c-2fecab43978c" :answer/id #uuid "52aebee7-a1be-5094-b50c-2fecab43978c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)≈-\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{x}{108}-\\frac{y}{108}-\\frac{z}{108}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8b357635-83ca-53f3-be6f-efc2212bf65c" :answer/id #uuid "8b357635-83ca-53f3-be6f-efc2212bf65c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)≈\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{x}{108}+\\frac{y}{54}+\\frac{z}{54}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4c8e5783-e729-5001-b425-9bd95d7f94c5" :answer/id #uuid "4c8e5783-e729-5001-b425-9bd95d7f94c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)≈\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{x}{108}-\\frac{y}{54}-\\frac{z}{54}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bac0b568-47cf-5aed-a2d1-d6ae3ec5aafb" :answer/id #uuid "bac0b568-47cf-5aed-a2d1-d6ae3ec5aafb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y,z)≈\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{x}{54}-\\frac{y}{54}-\\frac{z}{54}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4a523061-b982-5542-a530-946bca7d0e33" :question/id #uuid "4a523061-b982-5542-a530-946bca7d0e33" :question/math-academy-id "q-98552" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)=x{y}^{2}-1.$ Find the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(-2,-3).$" :question/worked-solution "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)≈f(a,b)+∇f(a,b)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(-2,-3)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ≈f(-2,-3)+∇f(-2,-3)\\cdot ⟨x+2,y+3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the definition of $f,$ we have that $f(-2,-3)=-19.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x} & ={y}^{2}\\, &  & ⇒\\,{f}_{x}(-2,-3)=(-3)^{2}=9, \\\\ {f}_{y} & =2xy &  & ⇒\\,{f}_{y}(-2,-3)=2(-2)(-3)=12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient of the function at the point $(-2,-3)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(-2,-3) & =⟨9,12⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the linear approximation of the function $f$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ≈f(-2,-3)+∇\\,f(-2,-3)\\cdot ⟨x+2,\\,y+3⟩ \\\\  & =-19+⟨9,12⟩\\cdot ⟨x+2,\\,y+3⟩ \\\\  & =-19+9(x+2)+12(y+3) \\\\  & =35+9x+12y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dbb4d8a0-1307-529a-b016-d7f1bd8d71e7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dbb4d8a0-1307-529a-b016-d7f1bd8d71e7" :answer-field/id #uuid "dbb4d8a0-1307-529a-b016-d7f1bd8d71e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2731dfc7-d2c6-5c2c-a042-6a0654dbb592" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fb391dd4-bbf2-513b-9210-bd1b8336cab0" "answer-7a449c97-159a-5f59-a721-89db59ab69e2" "answer-2731dfc7-d2c6-5c2c-a042-6a0654dbb592" "answer-a8fec697-0895-5a3c-96df-884cfd51b791" "answer-699fa767-12e0-5e62-9b8f-2b731f1a39e8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb391dd4-bbf2-513b-9210-bd1b8336cab0" :answer/id #uuid "fb391dd4-bbf2-513b-9210-bd1b8336cab0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)≈23+9x-6y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7a449c97-159a-5f59-a721-89db59ab69e2" :answer/id #uuid "7a449c97-159a-5f59-a721-89db59ab69e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)≈23-9x-6y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2731dfc7-d2c6-5c2c-a042-6a0654dbb592" :answer/id #uuid "2731dfc7-d2c6-5c2c-a042-6a0654dbb592" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)≈35+9x+12y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8fec697-0895-5a3c-96df-884cfd51b791" :answer/id #uuid "a8fec697-0895-5a3c-96df-884cfd51b791" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)≈35-9x+6y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-699fa767-12e0-5e62-9b8f-2b731f1a39e8" :answer/id #uuid "699fa767-12e0-5e62-9b8f-2b731f1a39e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x,y)≈41+6x+12y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-fd6c1f5e-0479-589e-8277-39b3bde8383f" :activity/id #uuid "fd6c1f5e-0479-589e-8277-39b3bde8383f" :activity/title "Linearization of Multivariable Functions" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049809 :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-439f497b-63cd-56ed-a071-521a6753dfc6" "step-e2dfefda-76b1-52f8-a7d5-688673b9ad6c" "step-d73be3e2-360c-5190-b3b2-da40bf0a43c4" "step-5ad6acc3-0cf4-512b-9839-fcc4716b1315" "step-5e7f4e61-c58d-5ffd-a813-3c6ffee4ea99"] :activity/first-step "step-439f497b-63cd-56ed-a071-521a6753dfc6" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-439f497b-63cd-56ed-a071-521a6753dfc6" :step/id #uuid "439f497b-63cd-56ed-a071-521a6753dfc6" :step/content "question-9d2fd7c0-6fec-5b30-98fe-3b0bf10ba9a4" :step/next "step-e2dfefda-76b1-52f8-a7d5-688673b9ad6c" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-e2dfefda-76b1-52f8-a7d5-688673b9ad6c" :step/id #uuid "e2dfefda-76b1-52f8-a7d5-688673b9ad6c" :step/content 17592186425853 :step/next "step-d73be3e2-360c-5190-b3b2-da40bf0a43c4" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-d73be3e2-360c-5190-b3b2-da40bf0a43c4" :step/id #uuid "d73be3e2-360c-5190-b3b2-da40bf0a43c4" :step/content "question-4a523061-b982-5542-a530-946bca7d0e33" :step/next "step-5ad6acc3-0cf4-512b-9839-fcc4716b1315" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-5ad6acc3-0cf4-512b-9839-fcc4716b1315" :step/id #uuid "5ad6acc3-0cf4-512b-9839-fcc4716b1315" :step/content 17592186404946 :step/next "step-5e7f4e61-c58d-5ffd-a813-3c6ffee4ea99" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-5e7f4e61-c58d-5ffd-a813-3c6ffee4ea99" :step/id #uuid "5e7f4e61-c58d-5ffd-a813-3c6ffee4ea99" :step/content 17592186265762 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054608 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-50989de1-e6f3-5831-87a9-51e32375a2a1" "question-4b607318-28df-51c2-9737-62f37f3092a8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-50989de1-e6f3-5831-87a9-51e32375a2a1" :question/id #uuid "50989de1-e6f3-5831-87a9-51e32375a2a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-68926" :question/problem "Calculate $(\\frac{2}{5}\\times {(-5)}^{2})÷({(-2)}^{5}-(-20)).$" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate this expression, we use PEMDAS.\n\nFirst, we consider the expressions inside each of the parentheses. The first one is.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5}\\times {(-5)}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying PEMDAS to this expression, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5}\\times {(-5)}^{2} & = \\\\ \\frac{2}{5}\\times 25 & = \\\\ \\frac{2}{5}\\times \\frac{25}{1} & = \\\\ \\frac{2\\times 25}{5\\times 1} & = \\\\ \\frac{50}{5} & = \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe expression inside the second parentheses is.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(-2)}^{5}-(-20).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying PEMDAS to this expression, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(-2)}^{5}-(-20) & = \\\\ (-32)+20 & = \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{2}{5}\\times {(-5)}^{2})÷({(-2)}^{5}-(-20)) & = \\\\ 10÷(-12) & = \\\\ \\frac{10}{(-12)} & = \\\\ -\\frac{10}{12} & = \\\\ -\\frac{5}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-eb165dbd-4e64-57b9-b591-6886c0a643cc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-eb165dbd-4e64-57b9-b591-6886c0a643cc" :answer-field/id #uuid "eb165dbd-4e64-57b9-b591-6886c0a643cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-27225eb8-4e94-5553-b530-1190a04b98a3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b2519c59-5675-54f8-9c49-fb9bd709992d" "answer-fb6ce3ab-bbde-5378-b4f8-47c8bd713822" "answer-5b6eb62b-0638-56b2-a12d-831896cfe037" "answer-27225eb8-4e94-5553-b530-1190a04b98a3" "answer-1a709506-d82a-59b7-a2b1-cc2efb6ccd0c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b2519c59-5675-54f8-9c49-fb9bd709992d" :answer/id #uuid "b2519c59-5675-54f8-9c49-fb9bd709992d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-120" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb6ce3ab-bbde-5378-b4f8-47c8bd713822" :answer/id #uuid "fb6ce3ab-bbde-5378-b4f8-47c8bd713822" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{120}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b6eb62b-0638-56b2-a12d-831896cfe037" :answer/id #uuid "5b6eb62b-0638-56b2-a12d-831896cfe037" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-27225eb8-4e94-5553-b530-1190a04b98a3" :answer/id #uuid "27225eb8-4e94-5553-b530-1190a04b98a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1a709506-d82a-59b7-a2b1-cc2efb6ccd0c" :answer/id #uuid "1a709506-d82a-59b7-a2b1-cc2efb6ccd0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4b607318-28df-51c2-9737-62f37f3092a8" :question/id #uuid "4b607318-28df-51c2-9737-62f37f3092a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-68934" :question/problem "Evaluate $(-3)\\times ((-8)^{2}\\times \\frac{3}{64}).$" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate this expression, we use PEMDAS.\n\nFirst, consider the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-8)^{2}\\times \\frac{3}{64}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying PEMDAS to this expression, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-8)^{2}\\times \\frac{3}{64} & = \\\\ 64\\times \\frac{3}{64} & = \\\\ \\frac{64}{1}\\times \\frac{3}{64} & = \\\\ \\frac{64\\times 3}{1\\times 64} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{64}\\times 3}{1\\times \\cancel{64}} & = \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-3)\\times ((-8)^{2}\\times \\frac{3}{64}) & = \\\\ (-3)\\times 3 & = \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-82dc6c2e-5b62-5fbc-aec5-c5800d42bb69"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-82dc6c2e-5b62-5fbc-aec5-c5800d42bb69" :answer-field/id #uuid "82dc6c2e-5b62-5fbc-aec5-c5800d42bb69" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bbb71dd0-6c77-5513-a284-fd4648420655" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bbb71dd0-6c77-5513-a284-fd4648420655" "answer-bce6cc9a-4320-5572-bbb9-66f3fdcad111" "answer-e7b1499b-0be4-535d-b32e-31dd5753c545" "answer-6dbec972-4ca4-5309-baad-353d47f0c0b4" "answer-16272320-c6ad-5fc2-84e3-d7dcf4eeabd8"] :db/ensure [:answer-fi